\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Up After Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  By Ctrl Bk \b0\par\par\uc2 783 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2001\par 13:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht ended up slightly against the U.S. dollar Monday on speculation that the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its lowest level in almost three and a half years in early trading. \par \par \uc2  Renewed strength in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  led by Indonesia's rupiah, which rallied in anticipation of the imminent removal of President Abdurrahman Wahid also supported the baht, traders said. Indonesia's National Assembly voted after the market's close to oust Wahid and appoint Vice-President Megawati Sukarnoputri in his place. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted in late trade at 45.76 baht, marginally down from THB45.775 at the Asian close Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar reached THB45.97 in early Sydney trade, in line with weakness in most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after emergency impeachment proceedings against Wahid began. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened in Bangkok around THB45.85-THB45.87 but heavy offers by Singapore dealers pushed the dollar back down to an intraday low of THB45.72. Traders said the move appeared to originate from institutions that usually acted on behalf of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The rumor on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spread all over the market, encouraging exporters to unload their dollars," a dealer at a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  However, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Pridiyathorn Devakula told reporters that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk was "just a rumor" and pure speculation. He added that the baht's fall early Monday was very brief, and was prompted by the uncertainty surrounding political developments in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  Renewed strength in most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly the Singapore dollar during the day, also helped support local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Pridiyathorn said the new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reporting forms should be ready before end-July, in line with previous expectations. \par \par \uc2  The new forms, which were to extend existing reporting rules for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions to nonresident accounts, have been under review since last month. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers expect the dollar to trade Tuesday in a THB45.70-THB45.90\par range, depending on the political situation in Indonesia.\par - - 23/07/01 11-15G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Government bond yields ended down slightly in very quiet trade Monday,\par in anticipation of the announcement of a long-term financing plan for\par the Financial Institutions Development Fund, or FIDF, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The October 2003 issue finished at 3.89%, down from a last deal Friday\par of 3.90%, while the December 2006 closed at 5.00%, down from 5.0025%,\par the Thai Bond Dealing Center said in its daily report.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Long-term bonds were mostly inactive Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As the market closed, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Pridiyathorn said the FIDF\par will issue THB320 billion in long-term, government-guaranteed bonds in\par the fourth quarter to finance its current short-term borrowings in the\par repurchase market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Another THB145 billion in FIDF bonds will be issued in 2003, THB151\par billion in 2004, and THB158 billion in 2005. Other upcoming FIDF issues\par will carry terms of six to 20 years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FIDF bonds issued during the current fiscal year to Sept. 30, with\par terms of two to five years, amounted to THB112 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Pridiyathorn said he would ensure that the large amount of bonds to be\par issued in the fourth quarter wouldn't have a big negative impact on the\par secondary bond market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He didn't elaborate, except to rule out the possibility of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  buying the bonds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There are ways but I can't tell you now," he told a news conference.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A dealer at a foreign bank said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would have to clarify\par how it will manage the fourth quarter issues before the market opens\par Tuesday, or news of the massive upcoming supply would have a big\par negative impact on both the secondary bond market and a scheduled FIDF\par auction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will offer THB2 billion worth of five-year FIDF bonds\par issued April 26. It will be the first of three auctions to offer the\par last THB8 billion unsold from April issues of two-year and five-year\par bonds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, overnight money market interest rates fell back from\par abnormally high levels reached Friday, when a few banks were caught\par short at the end of a biweekly reserve period.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Money market interest rates for terms of 14 days or more were mostly\par flat amid flush overall liquidity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market      Term                    Friday       Thursday\par Interbank  Overnight/Most Active    2.50%        2.75%\par Repurchase Overnight/Close          2.0000%      2.8125%\par            14-Day                   2.5000%      2.5000%\par            1-Month                  2.6250%      2.6250%\par            3-Month                  2.7500%      2.7500%\par -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266\par 0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com\par -0- 23/07/01 11-38G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010723dx7n000m4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
