\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Rupiah gets a boost but yen drags. \b0\par\par\uc2 866 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2001\par 10:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 23 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  parted ways late on Monday, with Taiwan and Korea wary of the yen and Southeast Asia spellbound by the Indonesian rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah climbed by over ten percent from late Friday levels around 11,138 as parliament geared itself to sack President Abdurrahman Wahid. \par \par \uc2  Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains were capped given the country's poor economic fundamentals, and its impact on the other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was muted as the rupiah market is limited to onshore. \par \par \uc2  Indonesian importers were also keen to take advantage of the cheaper dollar and helped cap further rupiah gains. \par \par \uc2  Falls in Japanese stocks to 16 year lows and weak economic data overshadowed lingering doubts over U.S. President George W. Bush's committment to the strong dollar policy. The yen found itself mired in the day's lows. \par \par \uc2  The yen's wobble sent shivers through North Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the Taiwan dollar facing data that provided more evidence of the island's slowing economy. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah jumped to a four-month high of 10,100 after foreign and local banks rushed to sell dollars as the country's political crisis headed towards a climax. \par \par \uc2  The Supreme Court ruled President Wahid's decree of a state of emergency was illegal and he could not disband the top assembly, which almost unanimously rejected his declaration. \par \par \uc2  The assembly's two main parties recommended the president be sacked, bringing his political demise one step closer. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the rupiah's rise was exaggerated by thin volumes and analysts doubted if the gains were sustainable as political and economic uncertainty linger. \par \par \uc2  Charts showed the dollar was massively oversold with a 14-day relative strength index reading at 3.8, suggesting scope for consolidation or correction. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia said it expected the rupiah to strengthen through 10,000 on expectations of improving political conditions. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht dipped to 45.97 - a whisker away from its 40-month low of 46.00 - before talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a firmer rupiah lifted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of its trough. \par \par \uc2  Offshore parties, especially Australian names, bought the dollar/baht actively in early trade as some investors use the baht as a hedging proxy for the less liquid rupiah. \par \par \uc2  A Japanese bank, which recently acted on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sold dollars soon after the baht hit its intraday low, sparking talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula denied having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, and market sources close to the deal said the Japanese bank's dollar sales were for customers and the amount was only around $20 million. \par \par \uc2  Pridiyathorn also said the authorities expected to finalise details of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reporting rules for non-residents before the end of July. The comment is likely to hold the market back from aggressively building up dollar positions for now. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar sank to 1.8310 before recouping lost ground on talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gains in the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also supported by tight liquidity in the money market, with the overnight rate remaining firm at around 3.50-4.00 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) was suspected to have been draining liquidity in the market to cap the Sing dollar's losses by not sterilising its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to keep its bearish tone in the near-term given underlying domestic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "The off-budget package to be announced this week will ease the pain of the downturn, but it will not materially impact on the economic growth this year," said a DBS report. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso bowed slightly to local corporate dollar demand, but wariness over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of President Gloria Arroyo's State of the Nation speech held speculators back. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said most players were acting on behalf of their corporate clients. Dollar sales in the afternoon session around 53.40 by foreign banks renewed talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  The government said it was working on issuing dollar-linked peso note with the aim of stabilising the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won tracked the yen lower, hovering around the day's low of 1,310.30 near the close. Sentiment was also dampened by sharp losses in local stocks. \par \par \uc2  Korea's benchmark KOSPI hit fresh three-month lows after dismal U.S. corporate results and forecasts. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said news of the government planning an economic stimulus package in the second half of this year to help ensure growth provided only mild support for the won as the amount is likely to be limited. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar braved through dismal economic data and downtrodden local stocks as players unwound their dollar longs in a market that has been long on dollar since July 5. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said the bad economic news had already been priced into the market. June export orders dropped by 19.92 percent on year while industrial output fell by 11.27 percent. \par \par \uc2  The unemployment rate set a new record in June, rising by 4.51 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010724dx7n00goc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
