\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Stuck in ranges, trade cautious. \b0\par\par\uc2 857 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2001\par 04:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 13 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lingered within familiar ranges early Friday in what is expected to be a cautious session ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2  Gains in U.S. stocks will help lend some support but surprisingly high weekly unemployment data and Argentina's financial woes will continue to cap any gains. \par \par \uc2  The debt crisis in Argentina, Latin America's third largest economy, has raised fears of emerging market contagion spreading to Asia. \par \par \uc2  Those concerns have however aided the yen against the dollar as investors unwinded carry trades in which they use the low-yield yen to invest in higher-yielding emerging market assets. \par \par \uc2  The yen was off its overnight 2-= week high against the dollar at the start of Tokyo trade but was still around 124, far from last week's lows around 126. \par \par \uc2  With nothing major on the local events calendar, players will focus on June U.S. retail sales and producer prices both due 1230 GMT and a consumer sentiment report from University of Michigan at 1300 GMT. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar edged back to 1.8340 having hit 11-year lows of 1.8398 on Thursday after the MAS shifted its stance to neutral from tightening to counter the economic downturn. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said local banks were offering U.S. dollars around 1.8350, stirring speculation they were acting on behalf of the authorities. They suspected the authorities have sold around $200 million when the Sing dollar spiked up on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  They added players were likely to square positions ahead of the weekend but U.S. funds were looking to buy dollars on dips from 1.8320-40. \par \par \uc2  The MAS said on Thursday it was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to dampen excessive volatility but said it does not normally comment on its market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO The peso was likely to come under pressure having hit fresh 5 1/2 month lows of 53.40 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said robust corporate demand from importers and jitters over possible spill-over damage from Argentina's financial turmoil would hurt sentiment. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said the bank did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT The baht was pinned just below 45.60, torn between importer dollar demand and fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said oil companies were looking to buy dollars around 45.50 but players are wary the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 45.85, 37-month lows hit on April 9. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was committed to keeping the baht stable and said it was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally to do so. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won edged down on continued equity-related outflows and on uncertainty over the yen's direction. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said gains in major U.S. tech companies after they raised revenue forecasts was likely to help overall sentiment. \par \par \uc2  But the upside was seen limited on an uncertain economic outlook at home and concerns about Argentina. \par \par \uc2  The won is still within an overall uptrend against the dollar since April 4, when it touched a low of 1,365.30 but has failed to strengthen past the 1,290 level since June 12. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was steady just a shade off the 35 mark on hopes the Nasdaq's overnight gains will boost equity-related inflows. \par \par \uc2  However, players looking at the worsening economic outlook and an easier \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rate stance on would continue to probe weaker levels for the Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  With parliamentary election due December 1, analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to allow a gradual exchange rate depreciation to help sagging growth and exports. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah kept within its well-worn range around 11,360 amid fading trading interest ahead of August impeachment hearings against President Abdurrahman Wahid. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said even the usually dollar-starved local corporates were keeping a low profile to avoid getting caught long or short in the run up to the special parliament session which will start the impeachment process. \par \par \uc2  Security concerns were heightened after at least 80 armed policemen and two armoured cars moved in on Thursday apparently to resist arrest of their rebel chief as ordered by President Wahid. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.24       124.39         +0.12\par  Sing dlr      1.8345       1.8328         -0.09\par  Taiwan dlr    34.951       34.976         +0.07\par  Korean won   1295.00      1296.00         +0.08\par  Baht           45.57        45.58         +0.02\par  Peso           53.17        53.05         -0.23\par  Rupiah      11365.00     11355.00         -0.09\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highligh