\par\par \b \uc2  Thai PM: No Plan To Change Repo Rate; Money Mkt Works \b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2001\par 05:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said Wednesday that there is no plan to change the 14-day repurchase rate after it was hiked by 100 basis points in early June. \par \par \uc2  Thaksin denied rumors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy board was planning to raise rates again. \par \par \uc2  "Prior to the repo rate hike, market mechanisms had been distorted. Now, market mechanisms are working well," Thaksin told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The monetary policy board will meet Thursday for a preliminary discussion ahead of its policy-setting meeting scheduled for July 19. \par \par \uc2  Thaksin said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aim in monitoring the baht is to ensure that the Thai unit moves in line with the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that volatility is limited. \par \par \uc2  A volatile baht could hurt exporters and importers and would also prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation, he said. \par \par \uc2  The baht has been fairly stable on fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula admitted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had entered the market in recent days to control liquidity as part of its regular \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Pridiyathorn has said the bank will manage the baht's float more actively. \par \par \uc2  At 0337 GMT (11:37 p.m. Tuesday EDT), the dollar was trading at 45.505 baht, up from THB45.470 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By 