\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Depressed as outlook worsens. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,078 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2001\par 10:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 10 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were easier late on Tuesday with the Singapore dollar and Taiwan dollar hitting new multi-year lows, depressed by poor economic data. \par \par \uc2  The yen also gave up some of its gains, but still managed to keep its distance from late Friday lows around 126. \par \par \uc2  But that was not enough for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  battered by slowing economies at home and abroad, and with little to suggest the slowdown had hit bottom. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar saw new 11-year lows after the government slashed its 2001 growth forecast as the economy shrank for the second straight quarter raising fears of a full-blown recession. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar fell to 34-month lows as second quarter export and import declines hit record levels. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the poor data had raised fears Singapore may announce a radical shift in its monetary policy at a review due Thursday, which would have consequences for other regionals especially the baht, rupiah and the peso. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar sank to fresh 11-year lows beyond 1.8370 on disappointing growth numbers. \par \par \uc2  Advance second quarter GDP data showed falls of 0.8 percent on-year and 10.1 percent on an annualised quarter-on-quarter basis, leaving Singapore in a technical recession. \par \par \uc2  The government slashed its 2001 growth forecast to 0.5-1.5 percent from 3.5-5.5 percent, adding to the gloom. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said European banks and U.S. investment banks were early sellers of the Sing dollar, with a further selloff by local banks pushed it to levels not seen since July 1990. \par \par \uc2  They cited sporadic corporate U.S. dollar offers at around 1.8370 but said players were looking to buy dollars on dips. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the dismal GDP data raised the prospect of the MAS shifting its bias to neutral from tightening at its mid-year policy review on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also focused on a parliamentary sitting on Wednesday when the government might raise the prospect of fiscal stimulus to counter the downturn. PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso came under pressure from weaker regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but avoided a damaging break of 53.10, 5-= month lows hit last week. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said telecom companies bought dollars near 52.85 with scattered dollar bids by importers lining up around 52.90 in otherwise thin trading. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said he did not expect the peso to deteriorate to between 55 and 60 in the next several months as predicted by some investment banks. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht held on to levels around 45.50 amid fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the regional weakness, especially the Singapore dollar's fall kept the dollar well bid around 45.40. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said foreign players were trimming dollar longs while local corporates and importers were bidding for dollars. \par \par \uc2  But caution prevailed after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed on Monday it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to shore up the baht. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said speculation about Thailand's commitment to a managed float had also kept foreign players cautious, despite repeated assurances by Thai officials they would stick to the current regime. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar touched a low of 34.759 with bearish trade data cementing views the authorities would guide the exchange rate lower to cushion the ailing economy. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave up its defence of the 34.50 level late Monday and had since only conducted smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the pace of the Taiwan dollar's decline. \par \par \uc2  June trade numbers showed exports shrinking 16.6 percent on the year, slightly better than market forecasts while imports contracted by a worse than expected 25.2 percent. \par \par \uc2  For the second quarter exports declined 17 percent and imports were down 22.8 percent on the year. Both were record quarterly declines. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won gave up its early gains as the yen came under pressure and as foreign investors continued to offload local stocks, raising concerns some of the sale proceeds may be converted into dollars. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors sold a net 81.6 billion won worth of shares on Tuesday after sales of 285 billion in the past two sessions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the falling Taiwan dollar and Singapore dollar also pressured the won. Taiwan and Singapore compete with Korea in several export sectors including electronics. \par \par \uc2  The won has failed to strengthen past the 1,290 level since June 12 but hopes of heavy investment flows in the second half have kept it in an overall uptrend since April 4, when it touched a low of 1,365.30. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah kept well within its week-old 11,225-11,375 per dollar range, with mild corporate dollar bids driving activity in a very thin market. \par \par \uc2  Political and economic worries continued to cloud the outlook, with the market shrugging off news Jakarta had reached agreement on almost all fronts with a visiting IMF mission. \par \par \uc2  Chief economics minister Burhannudin Abdullah said talks on controversial changes to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, the main sticking point in negotiations, had been deferred as sufficient compromise had been reached before the mission's arrival last Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Chartists said the rupiah could be headed for further losses if the dollar broke out of a constricting triangle dating back to early April on the weekly chart, and continued its uptrend. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia said the IMF expected it to further tighten monetary policy during certain periods, but added it would do so only if such a move would not hurt economic growth. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  #N/A DRP GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     125.65       125.51         -0.11\par  Sing dlr      1.8368       1.8283         -0.46\par  Taiwan dlr    34.656       34.545         -0.32\par  Korean won   1299.00      1296.20         -0.22\par  Baht           45.47        45.42         -0.11\par  Peso           52.94        52.84         -0.20\par  Rupiah      11355.00     11327.00         -0.25\par  Ringgit       3.7998       3.7995         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     125.65       114.45         -8.91\par  Sing dlr      1.8368       1.7365         -5.46\par  Taiwan dlr    34.656       32.900         -5.07\par  Korean won   1299.00      1277.00         -1.69\par  Baht           45.47        43.70         -3.89\par  Peso           52.94        50.75         -4.14\par  Rupiah      11355.00      9470.00        -16.60\par  Ringgit       3.7998       3.7995         -0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba00000200