\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mixed but economic worries weigh. \b0\par\par\uc2 971 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2001\par 04:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 10 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a mixed bag on Tuesday with some winning a brief reprieve from a steadier yen but others weighed down by the grim economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  In early Tokyo trade, the yen drifted away from Friday's lows around 126.15 as the dollar came under pressure from better-than-expected European and Japanese economic numbers. \par \par \uc2  Germany showed exports up by a surprising 16.5 percent on the year in April while Japanese machinery orders were down in May but not to troughs the market was expecting. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Federal Reserve said U.S. consumers in May borrowed at their slowest pace since the end of last year, indicating consumer spending was slowing. \par \par \uc2  Another reminder of a depressing economic outlook came from Singapore which slashed its growth outlook after weak advanced second quarter growth estimates. \par \par \uc2  With the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of the market, the Taiwan dollar slipped to fresh 34-month lows. Analysts believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was engineering an exchange rate decline to help boost sagging growth and exports. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar lapsed to a fresh 11-year low below 1.8310 after advance GDP figures released a flood of selling by interbank players. \par \par \uc2  Advance GDP growth for the second quarter fell 0.8 percent year-on-year. On an annualised quarter-on-quarter basis, it fell 10.1 percent, making a technical recession. \par \par \uc2  The government also cut its 2001 growth target to 0.5-1.5 percent from 3.5-5.5 percent. It said growth will remain weak in the third quarter, and only slow recovery will be seen in the fourth quarter. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said European banks and U.S. investment houses bought U.S. dollars from 1.8280, but fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  encouraged them to take profits at around 1.8300-10. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore is to announce its mid-year policy review on Thursday. Market views is divided over whether the MAS would shift its bias to neutral from tightening. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO The peso was pinned near 52.83 in thin morning trading, staying within striking distance from 5-= month lows of 53.10 hit last Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said volume has thinned since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  asked banks and corporates to use the non-deliverable forward market to cover future dollar needs. \par \par \uc2  They added any bounce in the peso would be met by fresh selling given the sluggish outlook for the domestic economy, a view shared by the IMF which said the Philippine was facing a challenging economic situation. \par \par \uc2  The IMF also said the country was vulnerable in its fiscal and banking sectors as well as externally. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht held onto around 45.45 but sentiment soured on the stumbling Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said oil and machinery importers are looking to buy dollars at around 45.40, but such bids are running into offers by players who fear possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the baht last week, when it hit 10-week lows of 45.70. Dealers have estimated the bank had sold at least $100 million. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won edged higher in line with the yen and on hopes foreign equity investors may halt their sale of local stocks after the Nasdaq's overnight gains. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said settlement of stocks sold by foreign investors in recent sessions would cap any significant gains. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors have sold a net 285 billion won worth of local shares in the past two sessions. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Korea will release June import and export prices at 0300 GMT. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar fell to fresh 34-month lows as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled out of the market indicating it will allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to settle in a weaker band. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar hit 34.70, seen in early September 1998, before exporters came in prompting other players to book profits on the U.S. dollar's gains. \par \par \uc2  Charts also suggest the U.S. dollar was due for some profit-taking, with the 14-day relative strength index showing a reading of 83.19. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had defended the 34.50 level for the past six weeks after engineering its fall from around the 33 level in May. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah edged down to 11,350 as local corporates were back with fresh dollar orders after most of them had covered their rupiah requirements for tax payments. \par \par \uc2  A survey showed business sentiment has slipped further in April-May due to grim economic outlook and shaky politics. \par \par \uc2  A bi-monthly survey by state brokerage Danareksa showed its business sentiment index - which incorporates conditions for the present situation and six months ahead - dropped to 110.1 from 113.8 in February-March and 115.3 in January-February. \par \par \uc2  A reading above 100 denotes positive responses outnumbered negative ones. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     125.44       125.51         +0.06\par  Sing dlr      1.8310       1.8283         -0.15\par  Taiwan dlr    34.677       34.545         -0.38\par  Korean won   1294.20      1296.20         +0.15\par  Baht           45.47        45.42         -0.11\par  Peso           52.86        52.83         -0.06\par  Rupiah      11345.00     11327.00         -0.16\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.8000         +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     125.44       114.45         -8.76\par  Sing dlr      1.8310       1.7365         -5.16\par  Taiwan dlr    34.677       32.900         -5.12\par  Korean won   1294.20      1277.00         -1.33\par  Baht           45.47        43.70         -3.89\par  Peso           52.86        50.75         -3.99\par  Rupiah      11345.00      9470.00        -16.53\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.8000         +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010710dx7a004bo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
