\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets - Stocks suffer, no solace for  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2      By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 967 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2001\par 12:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 9 (Reuters) - Asian equities suffered a \par \par \uc2  downbeat session on Monday as investor unease over corporate \par \par \uc2  earnings soured the market's already rampant pessimism about \par \par \uc2  the economic outlook. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In Tokyo, the benchmark Nikkei average         fell more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par than two percent at one stage, hit by concerns about high-tech\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par earnings.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But it trimmed losses in the afternoon after Japan's core\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par private-sector machinery orders fell a less-than-expected 2.1\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in May from a month ago, giving a crumb of comfort to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I would hesitate to describe it as a source of optimism,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ING Barings economist Richard Jerram said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "My concern in general is that profits drive machinery\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par orders and profits are clearly taking a beating at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par moment... So I view it as more of a temporary respite more than\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par anything."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Japanese government bonds (JGBs) also headed south as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors bet banks would cover equity losses by selling bonds\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to window-dress their half-year bookclosings in September.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     So yields on the benchmark 232nd 10-year cash JGBs\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  rose 10 basis points to 1.345 percent, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par highest level since April 26, before paring gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market was also wary the government might have to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par implement a supplementary budget to support the economy, which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it would need to fund by issuing extra bonds with the budget\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deep in the red.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen        was taking a breather at 125.54 having\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buckled to three-month troughs of 126.15 late on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SING DOLLAR IN THROES\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen's latest spasm left a scar on regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the Singapore dollar a major casualty.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It kept a softer tone at 1.8280 per dollar, within striking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par distance of 1.8290, the fresh 11-year low hit late on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers warned of more pain ahead for the Sing dollar as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the evidence of a slowing economy is emerging at an alarming\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pace.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The government releases second-quarter growth figures on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday, which analysts said could contain the seeds for a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par further decline.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore is due to announce its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mid-year policy review on Wednesday, as some argue the need for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par an easier stance to weather the slowdown.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the market view is still divided over whether the MAS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would actually shift its tightening bias to neutral, guiding\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Sing dollar to weaken on a trade-weighted basis.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Monetary policy is aimed very much at trade-weighted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (targets), which means even if they keep to their modest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appreciation stance, the dollar/Sing can still head higher,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Philip Wee, regional markets and treasury strategist at DBS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank, told Reuters television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Wee said the Sing dollar's weakness was in line with other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and domestic interest rates are low.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "So you don't really need to see any change in the stance."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Wee expected the Sing dollar to reach 1.83 to 1.84 if the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen slips further to 135 or 140.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BAHT WINS REPRIEVE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht        has settled around 45.44 but failed to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stretch higher even after baht funding costs in the offshore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market eased.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The one-month forward rate edged down to 25/45 satang per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar having shot up to 40/60 earlier from around 12 a week\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bangkok dealers said the baht was torn between dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buying demand by importers and fears of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Anxiety about possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  intensified after Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula confirmed the bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the baht last week to keep the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stable.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers have estimated the bank had sold at least $100\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million last Thursday when it hit 10-week lows of 45.70.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts said uncertainties surrounding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reporting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rules would support the baht, but they saw it was unlikely to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pop up above 45 as underlying concerns about the economy would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weigh on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0921 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     125.51       125.77         +0.21\par  Sing dlr      1.8283       1.8256         -0.15\par  Taiwan dlr    34.545       34.473         -0.21\par  Korean won   1296.20      1289.00         -0.56\par  Baht           45.42        45.40         -0.04\par  Peso           52.83        52.86         +0.06\par  Rupiah      11327.00     11335.00         +0.07\par  Ringgit       3.8000       3.7995         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     125.51       114.4