\par\par \b \uc2  Thai c.bank confirms  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  on baht. \b0\par\par\uc2 104 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2001\par 07:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 9 (Reuters) - Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula confirmed on Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the baht last week. \par \par \uc2  He told reporters that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable but would not try to resist the regional trend. Pridiyathorn said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Thursday in support of the baht. \par \par \uc2  He said the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not abnormal. \par \par \uc2  "It is not unusual. We would not resist the market and will move in line with the regional trend. Baht trading should not be too volatile," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010709dx7900at5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
