\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Up Amid Talk Of Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2001\par 13:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht ended slightly higher against the U.S. dollar Thursday as rumors of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  triggered heavy dollar selling in the afternoon session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 45.45 baht, slightly down from THB45.48 at the Asian close Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit rose to a high of THB45.67 in early trade as the yen weakened. \par \par \uc2  "In early afternoon, there was dollar selling pressure which started offshore. The market suspected that there might have been some kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though there's no confirmation from the authorities," said a dealer at a major local bank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumored to have sold a total of $100 million to $200 million via Thai banks and brokers in Bangkok and a Japanese bank in Singapore, dealers in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a local bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to soak up liquidity in offshore swap markets, driving up implied yields and forcing investors to rush to cover short-baht positions. \par \par \uc2  Dollar buying on dips by local corporates, however, helped bring the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  off a low of THB45.42, dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  assistant governor Chettavee Charoenpitaks declined to comment on speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Chetthavee said Thursday that the bank wasn't concerned by the baht's recent weakness, as it was in line with the trend in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the yen's decline. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be closely monitoring the market for any irregular movements, he said. \par \par \uc2  Chettavee said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will speed up its review of new transaction reporting requirements, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses to monitor capital flows and compliance with restrictions on baht outflows, but he declined to say when it might be completed. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said earlier this week that the review will be completed by the end of July. Many investors remained sidelined by the ongoing uncertainty over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intentions. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is expected to open Monday in a range of THB45.40-THB45.70. \par \par \uc2  Thai markets will be closed Friday for a public Buddhist holiday. \par \par \uc2  Government bond yields closed mixed Thursday, as investors continued to buy very short-term issues, while selling pressure slightly outweighed buying in the longer issues, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The issue due December 2008 closed at 5.43%, up from a last deal Wednesday of 5.42%, while the October 2003 issue finished at 3.95%, down from 4.01%, said the Thai Bond Dealing Center in its daily report. Yields move in the opposite direction to prices. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment remains fragile, because although the finance ministry has said it won't issue government bonds in the current quarter, new supply could be very heavy once issuance resumes. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market interest rates rose on demand for cash ahead of the long weekend and pressure from implied yields in the onshore \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap market, which rose due to recent weakness in the baht. \par \par \uc2  Longer rates were mostly stable amid generally flush liquidity. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market       Term                    Thursday     Wednesday\par Interbank   Overnight/Most Active    2.75%        2.375%\par Repurchase  Overnight/Close          2.5000%      2.4375%\par             14-Day                   2.5000%      2.5000%\par             1-Month                  2.6250%      2.6250%\par             3-Month                  2.8125%      2.8125%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Phisanu Phromchanya and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266\par 0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx75032uw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
