\par\par \b \uc2  Thai economist favours flexible baht regime. \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2001\par 12:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 4 (Reuters) - A key economic adviser to Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said on Wednesday he favoured a managed but flexible regime for the Thai baht, a position in line with the policy pursued by the Thai authorities. Former Thai Finance Minister Virabongsa Ramangkula told a seminar he believed the Bank of Thailand should adopt a policy on the baht that would neither be based on a fixed exchange rate nor on a full free float. \par \par \uc2  "The appropriate exchange rate should be based on any regime that is not pegged to a particular \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , nor should it be a 100 percent free float. It should be a managed float regime," he said. \par \par \uc2  Virabongsa surprised financial markets earlier this week by telling a local newspaper in an interview that Thailand should consider pegging the baht to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a means of stabilising its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Thai language daily Krungthep Thurakij on Tuesday quoted Virabongsa as calling on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to devise a new system to manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid the volatility of recent months. \par \par \uc2  He told the paper that the new system would be a balance between the current "managed float" regime, under which the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOT) lets the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float freely but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow big movements, and a fixed rate system. \par \par \uc2  The suggestion was quickly dismissed by Thai authorities with both BOT Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula and Thai Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak saying the baht level should be set by market forces and they would stick to their current policy of a "managed float" for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Virabongsa said on Wednesday a fixed rate for the baht would pit Thailand against market forces, while a complete free float would expose Thai businesses to increased \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks and erode their competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  "There should be (\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate) management but not under a set, inflexible regime," the economist said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht stood at around 45.50 per dollar on Wednesday afternoon, down from around 43 at the beginning of the year. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx74007rl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
