\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Thailand says no plans to peg  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Vithoon Amorn \par \uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2001\par 09:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 3 (Reuters) - Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor and finance minister on Tuesday brushed aside speculation the country might follow the advice of an influential economist who says the baht should be pegged to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula and Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said the authorities had no plans to abandon the current managed float regime for the baht. \par \par \uc2  Somkid told reporters the Thai authorities would focus on maintaining baht stability without changing the exchange rate policy. \par \par \uc2  Pridiyathorn said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the baht was too volatile, but that the country would retain a managed float system. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said recent statements by Pridiyathorn and Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra that the baht should move in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had prompted baht selling. \par \par \uc2  The baht retreated on Tuesday, standing at around 45.37 per dollar at 0626 GMT against 45.29 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In his Tuesday comments Pridiyathorn said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would this month finalise changes in rules on reporting \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deals. He said the changes would not create an excessive back office burden for banks handling such transactions. \par \par \uc2  Speculation Thaksin's government was considering some kind of capital controls has mounted in recent months but has been repeatedly denied by the authorities. \par \par \uc2  ADVISER CALLS FOR PEGGED BAHT \par \par \uc2  Former Finance Minister Virabongsa Ramangkula, an economist and a top adviser to Thaksin, was quoted on Tuesday in Thai-language daily Krungthep Thurakij as saying Thailand should devise a new system to manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid the volatility of recent months. \par \par \uc2  The new system would be a balance between the current "managed float" regime, under which the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  lets the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float freely but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow big movements, and a fixed rate system. \par \par \uc2  "It might not be appropriate for Thailand to return to the old fixed rate system as it would expose us to market attacks like in the past. But at the same time, insisting on maintaining a managed float regime would restrict our economic growth," he said. \par \par \uc2  "The solution is for Thailand to find a new exchange rate system that would be a balance between a managed float and a fixed exchange rate." \par \par \uc2  He said that under this proposal, the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would allow the baht to fluctuate within a band of perhaps 10 percent. \par \par \uc2  The exact size of this band would be kept confidential, to avoid offering \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators a target, he said. \par \par \uc2  "This is to keep the exchange rate stable and help the private sector save the cost of managing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks," he said. \par \par \uc2  Until mid-1997, Thailand operated a system of bands against the dollar. The system was abandoned on July 2, 1997 after sustained selling pressure by \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht, based on its real effective exchange rate (REER) that measures its trade weighted competitiveness relative to \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other developing countries, should head lower against the dollar after recent falls in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A senior dealer at a foreign bank said comments by the governor and finance minister had assured the market the baht exchange rate policy would remain unchanged in the short term. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx7300e4b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
