\par\par \b \uc2  Top Thai economist wants baht pegged - paper. \b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2001\par 05:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 3 (Reuters) - An influential Thai economist is urging Thailand to consider pegging the baht to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a means of stabilising the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a Thai newspaper reported on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Former Finance Minister Virabongsa Ramangkula, a top adviser to Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra, told Thai language daily Krungthep Thurakij that Thailand should devise a new system to manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid the volatility of recent months. \par \par \uc2  The new system would be a balance between the current "managed float" regime, under which the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  lets the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float freely but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow big movements, and a fixed rate system. \par \par \uc2  Virabongsa told Krungthep Thurakij in the interview: \par \par \uc2  "It might not appropriate for Thailand to return to the old fixed rate system as it would expose us to market attacks like in the past. But at the same time, insisting on maintaining a managed float regime would restrict our economic growth. \par \par \uc2  "The solution is for Thailand to find a new exchange rate system that would be a balance between a managed float and a fixed exchange rate," he said. \par \par \uc2  Virabongsa said an alternative regime which the Asian Development Bank had considered would be for the baht to be pegged against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of regional and major trading partners, not just against the U.S. dollar like in the past. \par \par \uc2  He said that under this proposal, the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would allow the baht to fluctuate within a band of perhaps 10 percent. \par \par \uc2  The exact size of this band would be kept confidential, to avoid offering \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators a target, he said. \par \par \uc2  "This is to keep the exchange rate stable and help the private sector save the cost of managing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks," he said. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said on Tuesday he had no plans to return the baht to a fixed exchange rate regime but his bank would be ready to enter the market to stabilise the baht. \par \par \uc2  Until mid-1997, Thailand operated a system of bands against the U.S. dollar. The system was abandoned on July 2, 1997 after sustained selling pressure by \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's decision to allow the baht to float helped trigger the Asian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx7300d46\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
