\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Snug in ranges as dollar/yen stable. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2001\par 11:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 7 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  endured another rangebound session on Thursday, as the dollar and yen played tug-of-war over a small bit of turf. \par \par \uc2  Local developments also failed to generate much excitement. As widely expected, the Bank of Korea held its overnight call rate steady at five percent while investors in Manila shrugged off the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to also hold off on further rate cuts. \par \par \uc2  Poor trade data failed to ruffle the Taiwan dollar. And the Thai baht saw relatively tame trading in a market wary of the Bank of Thailand's next move. \par \par \uc2  For now, the yen had the upper hand against the dollar as it gained on the sterling ahead of the British general election. Investors were banking on a victory by the ruling Labour Party, which is expected to hold a referendum on joining the euro and engineer a much more competitive exchange rate before conversion. \par \par \uc2  But both the dollar and yen were facing negative factors, with the yen suffering from economic uncertainty and the dollar upset by a letter from U.S. trade groups to Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill complaining about the strong dollar. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was strait-jacketed in a narrow 45.14-45.34 range as dollar sales by funds and interbank players were countered by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula confirmed on Thursday that the authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Wednesday, but declined to elaborate. \par \par \uc2  There were rumours in the market on Wednesday that the BOT spent $100-200 million to buy the dollar from 44.80 to curb the baht's rapid rise and to build up its foreign reserves. \par \par \uc2  "The message is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do what it needs to keep the baht stable. And they bought the dollar at pretty good levels. So they managed to slow down the baht's rise which could hurt exports and replenish their reserves at the same time," said a Bangkok dealer. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said the baht's downside was likely to be limited at around 45.50 in the near-term as foreign funds who were long of dollars sought to trim their positions, believed to be in the billions. \par \par \uc2  Baht liquidity remained flush in the short-end, with the one-month forward rate quoted at 3/5 satang per dollar offshore and -2.5/0 satang onshore. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won ended nearly flat from Tuesday's close of 1,286.7. Seoul markets were closed on Wednesday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said trading was light, and the market ignored a widely expected decision by the Bank of Korea to hold its overnight call rate steady at five percent due to concerns over rising inflation. \par \par \uc2  Charts showed the dollar/won has been on a downtrend since it hit a high of 1,265.3 on April 4, coinciding with the dollar/yen's move lower. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the won's gains were capped around 1,280, with importers interested in buying dollars around that area. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar did not stray far from a tidy range of 34.031-34.080 despite grim economic data. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier May exports fell by 22.6 percent on year, while imports fell by 29.6 percent on year. Both figures were much worse than expected. \par \par \uc2  But Singapore dealers said activity was dull as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been spotted on both sides of the market. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah shuffled around the 11,200 mark, enjoying a spell of stability, but its gains were capped near 11,000 as local corporates continued to snatch up dollars on dips. \par \par \uc2  Charts showed the dollar/rupiah staying within a range of 10,800-11,450 as fears of political violence died down after parliament voted to convene a special session to decide whether to impeach President Abdurrahman Wahid. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say while the rupiah may climb if Wahid is deposed in a peaceful manner, its rise would be short-lived given Indonesia's huge economic problems. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the government insisted on a parliamentary debate over controversial \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  amendments, which have impeded negotiations with the IMF over the resumption of lending. \par \par \uc2  Chief economic minister Rizal Ramli said it would be difficult for the government to keep 2001 inflation below 10 percent following its decision to raise prices in key sectors. The government's proposed budget revisions to parliament have assumed inflation this year would hit 9.3 percent. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar was slightly firmer in quiet trade, keeping well within its 1.80-1.82 range of the past three weeks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was still looking to buy the U.S. dollar on dips to around 1.8060 - its Wednesday low - due to the weak economic outlook for Singapore and the region. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S dollar/Sing dollar is expected to remain in the 1.80-1.82 trading range, barring a major weakening of the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We expect a year-end level of around 1.78," said a DBS report. \par \par \uc2  DBS based its year-end forecast on an assumption that the economy would turn around in the last quarter, with growth picking up to around 3.6 percent on the year in the fourth quarter from 1.8 percent expected in the third quarter. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The Philippine market was locked in a tight 50.50-50.78 range in what dealers described as an "uneventful" market. \par \par \uc2  "Little has happened in the market today. There are no strong leads, and only around $83 million was transacted compared with around $143 million yesterday," said a Manila dealer, adding that the second quarter was normally a slow period for trade. \par \par \uc2  The rebel saga weighed on sentiment, but did not move the market much as investors expected it to be a protracted story. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its key overnight rates unchanged, saying it would prefer to wait for more economic data before taking action. The borrowing rate is at 9.0 percent and the lending rate at 11.25 percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0904 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     119.86\tab  120.50\tab    +0.53\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8092\tab  1.8117\tab    +0.14\par  Taiwan dlr    34.065\tab  34.065\tab    +0.00\par  Korean won   1287.50\tab 1286.00\tab    -0.12\par  Baht\tab      45.08\tab   45.18\tab    +0.22\par  Peso\tab      50.69\tab   50.72\tab    +0.06\par  Rupiah\tab 11140.00     11185.00\tab    +0.40\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.86\tab  114.45\tab    -4.51\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8092\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.02\par  Taiwan dlr    34.065\tab  32.900\tab    -3.42\par  Korean won   1287.50\tab 1277.00\tab    -0.82\par  Baht\tab      45.08\tab   43.70\tab    -3.06\par  Peso\tab      50.69\tab   50.75\tab    +0.12\par  Rupiah\tab 11140.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -14.99\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6702bly\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
