\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Lower; Upcoming  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Rules Support \b0\par\par\uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2001\par 13:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht finished slightly lower Friday as importers took the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent gains on concerns over possible changes in Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy as an opportunity to buy U.S. dollars on weakness, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at 45.36 baht, slightly up from THB45.33 at the Asian close Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Intraday weakness in the Japanese yen also weighed on the baht, but the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended off a late low of THB45.50 to the dollar on jitters related to a meeting between the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and financial institutions. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand met bank officials Friday to explain new reporting requirements for transactions involving nonresident accounts, which will be implemented July 2. \par \par \uc2  The tightened reporting requirements are to improve the ability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to monitor capital flows and compliance with existing controls on baht outflows. \par \par \uc2  Concerns that current limited capital controls will be tightened have heightened since incoming \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula, who is expected to take office next week, said late Wednesday that he is mulling a package of measures to limit capital outflows. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials declined to comment on any changes in policy or organization which might occur after reviews conducted by the new governor. \par \par \uc2  Uncertainty supported the baht Friday, and should continue to do so until Pridiyathorn's intentions are clearer. \par \par \uc2  Comments from Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak Friday injected more uncertainty into the situation. He said monetary and fiscal policy won't be changed. \par \par \uc2  He also added that balance of payment deficits should be prevented and that the government's economic policy would focus on stability rather than growth. The latter comments could signal an increase in interest rates or a further tightening of capital controls. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the baht to open in a range of THB45.30-THB45.60 per dollar Monday. \par \par \uc2  Thai government bond yields dropped 10 to 30 basis points Friday as continued buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  finally convinced the market to participate in a partial recovery after the 90- to 100-basis point increases seen early in the week, dealers said. Yields move in the opposite direction to prices. \par \par \uc2  Ongoing uncertainty over the intentions of Pridiyathorn on interest rates should limit any further gains until he completes a review of monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  The incoming governor has scheduled a press conference for 0400 GMT Monday (12:00 a.m. Monday EDT), but he isn't expected to provide explicit guidance on interest rates. Officials have said rates controlled by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain low, but may rise slightly. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the government bond due December 2008 dropped to 5.37% from 5.65%, after rising sharply Thursday, while the issue due December 2006 finished at 4.90%, down from 5.17%, the Thai Bond Dealing Center said in its daily report. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped to set a yield for the bond due April 2002 at 2.50%, after the market failed to close a deal on the issue Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The overnight interbank interest rate continued to decline from the highs they reached earlier in the week after the news of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor's replacement broke Monday, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to inject funds through the repurchase market. Other money market rates were mostly flat. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market       Term                       Friday     Thursday\par Interbank   Overnight/Most Active       2.0000%    2.5000%\par Repurchase  Overnight/Close             1.3125%    1.3125%\par             14-Day                      1.5000%    1.5000%\par             1-Month                     1.8125%    1.8125%\par             3-Month                     1.9375%    1.9375%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Phisanu Phromchanya and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266\par 0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx6102ixs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
