\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Dented by Wall Street, China B-shares buck trend. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Nick Edwards \par \uc2 1,251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2001\par 12:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      HONG KONG, May 31 (Reuters) - Asian asset prices were \par \par \uc2  pressured on Thursday by a technology-led sell-off on Wall \par \par \uc2  Street which dented stocks and left investors mulling the \par \par \uc2  potential for more gloom ahead in the region's export oriented \par \par \uc2  economies. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     South Korea\tab    and Hong Kong\tab   equities were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hardest hit in the region with benchmark indices falling 2.6\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and 1.8 percent respectively.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Japan's bellwether Nikkei 225\tab    was shaken down 1.7\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent by a tumble on the U.S. Nasdaq and a bout of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investment ratings downgrades of high-profile telecoms and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high-tech firms.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro lurched lower to around 101.39 yen\tab      in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late afternoon trade, compared with around 103.00 in morning\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade, and its weakness translated into dollar strength in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen , which climbed to 119.16 against the greenback.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TECH WOES HIT STOCKS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Hong Kong blue chips were led lower by China Mobile\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  as investors feared further profit warnings from U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tech firms.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Turnover stood at HK$15.98 billion (US$2.05 billion), the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par highest in more than a month. Declines outnumbered advances 325\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 192, with 233 stocks unchanged.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Earnings warnings from U.S. tech companies sent the Nasdaq\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par spiralling down more than four percent overnight.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     China Mobile, the top mainland cellular carrier and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hang Seng's second largest constituent, ended 2.83 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     South Korean shares closed more than two percent lower as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors eschewed tech stocks, beating down chip maker Samsung\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Electronics to a two-week low.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     CHINA B-SHARES BUCK TREND\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     China's hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  B-shares bucked the faltering trend,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bolstered by investors banking on another wave of liquidity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par flowing into the markets with the end of a ban on using \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deposited since February 19 to buy shares.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some analysts estimated $2-$3 billion in deposits -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par amounting to 10 to 15 percent of the overall market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par capitalisation - could flow into B shares over the next month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after the restriction is lifted on June 1.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Shanghai B share index closed up 2.61 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at 239.731 points after touching a record high of 241.305 in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late trade. Turnover rose to a huge $582.03 million from an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par already heavy $493.17 million on Wednesday. Shanghai's B-share\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par index is up 168 percent so far this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Shenzhen's B index inched up 0.50 percent to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 425.51. Turnover rose to HK$2.23 billion from a heavy HK$2.18\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Most of these stocks can potentially double...the existing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par valuation gap is about 42 percent and I see a lot of B-share\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prices exceeding their A-share prices," Joe Zhang, head of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China research at UBS Warburg in Hong Kong, told Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government opened the formerly foreigners-only B share\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets to Chinese investors in late February, but in a bid to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exclude black market money it barred the use of hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deposited after February 19.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 THAILAND\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NOT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENING\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Deputy Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Pakorn Malakul na\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Ayutthaya said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the baht, which has gained against the dollar this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Pakorn said the BOT injected about 20 billion baht into the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par repo market in the past two days in order to prevent sharp\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par volatility of short-term interest rates after the government\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fired \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the local money market had tightened this week as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reflected by a sharp rise in government bond yields. But\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par analysts say the baht's recovery could be short-lived.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "In the long run you simply cannot have interest rates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower than the U.S. interest rate and have a strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Steven Xu, senior economist at SG Securities in Hong Kong told\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Xu said steepening the yield curve to help recapitalisation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of banks badly mauled by Asia's financial crisis had negative\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par implications for the baht and asset prices in Thailand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We could see a period of artificial strength of the baht,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but then something has to give and that means you're going to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par see greater inflation coming through in the economy and you're\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par going to see lower stock/asset valuations," Xu said. The baht\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was quoted at 45.30 to the U.S. dollar in late Asian trade. It\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has appreciated about 0.9 percent after hitting a low of 45.64\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ABSENCE OF VIOLENCE HELPS RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah gained over one percent with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market relieved over the absence of serious violence after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par parliament voted to hold a special session to decide whether to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par impeach President Abdurrahman Wahid.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ended off an intra-day high of 10,925, but was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still firm as players unwound dollar longs, triggering\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stop-loss dollar sales around 11,100.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts say the rupiah may spike higher if there is a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par peaceful transition of power, but it would soon run aground due\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to Indonesia's mountain of foreign debt.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Probably before August we are going to see political\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par clarity, we are going to see strong leadership coming through\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in Jakarta. That's going to boost market confidence and I\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wouldn't be surprised if the Indonesian rupiah strengthened to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par somewhere between 9,000 and 10,000 in the short term," SG's Xu\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Then we need to see drastic action taken by industrial\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par countries like Japan and the U.S. because we do need a sort of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par debt forgiveness programme... otherwise the country is in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par insolvency perpetually," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0944 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     118.98\tab  120.06\tab    +0.91\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8085\tab  1.8060\tab    -0.14\par  Taiwan dlr     33.90\tab   34.01\tab    +0.33\par  Korean won   1282.50\tab 1289.00\tab    +0.51\par  Baht\tab  