\par\par \b \uc2  Thai PM: Weak THB No Worry As Ctrl Bk Monitoring Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2001\par 07:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said Tuesday he isn't concerned about the recent weakness in the baht because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely monitoring the market. \par \par \uc2  Thaksin said local exporters were taking the opportunity to boost exports while the baht is weak. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had dropped from around 45.65 baht to the dollar at the Asian open Tuesday to around THB45.50, after the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was said to have joined a selling spree triggered by the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's early slide against the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  The market took Thaksin's midday comments as a reaffirmation that the government favors a weak baht policy to boost exports and pushed the dollar up to test THB45.60. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect a range of THB45.50 to THB45.65 to hold Tuesday, however, because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, and it has confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around these levels last week. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to be comfortable with a gradual depreciation in line with movement of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, but it closely monitors trade for speculative activity. \par \par \uc2  Restrictions on baht outflows are used to limit supply offshore, raising the cost of borrowing baht to cover short positions to punishing levels whenever speculators gang up on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Phisanu Phromchanya, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744;\par phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com\par -0- 10/04/01 06-03G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx4a01o3i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
