\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk: Baht Volatility Mostly On Dollar-Yen Moves \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2001\par 07:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday that recent volatility in the baht was mostly due to the movement of the U.S. dollar against the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  Chettavee Charoenpitaks, Bank of Thailand assistant governor for financial markets \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told reporters that the authorities are closely monitoring baht trade in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In response to questions about a local newspaper article alleging that\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would develop new capital controls, Chettavee said he\par wasn't aware of any such plans.\par - - 09/04/01 05-38G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chettavee said that Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies leave the market\par well controlled and that there is no need for any new measures.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of Thailand restricts the flow of baht to offshore markets in\par order to raise the cost of covering short-baht positions by borrowing in\par offshore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Local dealers are required to name parties and define the purpose of\par all \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions, helping the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to monitor\par capital flows and compliance.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the offshore spot, forward and swap\par markets last week to further dry up liquidity and slow the baht's\par decline.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But officials have said repeatedly that most of the recent volatility\par was due to the dollar's rise against the yen and other regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and that there has been no abnormal speculative activity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chettavee said the baht has also received some support from the\par country's economic fundamentals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If domestic confidence is good, the baht shouldn't weaken much\par further, Chettavee said, without specifying how far the baht might\par weaken or which aspects of the domestic economy were supportive.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts expect the baht to weaken slowly until U.S. and global demand\par for Thai exports begins to recover later in the year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At midday Monday, the dollar was trading at 37-month highs between\par THB45.80 and THB45.83, up from a range of THB45.60 to THB45.65 late\par Friday in Asian trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Phisanu Phromchanya, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744;\par phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx4901ll9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
