\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets - Nasdaq gives stocks some lift,  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  glum. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 1,029 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2001\par 11:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, April 6 (Reuters) - Asian stocks danced to the \par \par \uc2  Nasdaq's upbeat tune on Friday in early trade, but lost some \par \par \uc2  energy as the day wore on and doubts developed about whether \par \par \uc2  U.S. gains would be sustained. \par \par \uc2      Most closed firmer but well off their highs. \par \par \uc2      Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stumbled alongside the yen after \par \par \uc2  euphoria surrounding a new Japanese economic package quickly \par \par \uc2  fizzled out. \par \par \uc2      Tech-heavy Korean and Taiwan markets rose after the Nasdaq \par \par \uc2  jumped 8.92 percent or 146.20 points to close at 1,785.00 \par \par \uc2  overnight -- its biggest percentage gains ever. \par \par \uc2      U.S. market sentiment had been boosted by news Dell \par \par \uc2  Computer Corp stood by its first-quarter targets. \par \par \uc2      The Korean Composite Stock Price Index (KOSPI) ended 2.54 \par \par \uc2  percent or 12.53 points higher at 506.22. Taiwan's TAIEX gained \par \par \uc2  2.02 percent on the Nasdaq's rally and signs of easing \par \par \uc2  U.S.-China tensions. \par \par \uc2  Japan's stocks closed off their intraday's high after a \par \par \uc2  long-awaited emergency economic package designed to boost the \par \par \uc2  country's growth and stock market came in short on detail. \par \par \uc2  "The package looks fairly solid - it just left too many \par \par \uc2  questions unanswered to warrant a broad-based advance," said \par \par \uc2  Nobuaki Kurisu, chief fund manager at Sumisei Global Investment \par \par \uc2  Trust Management. \par \par \uc2  The next event for market focus is the all-important U.S. \par \par \uc2  job report to be released later in the day, for a clue to U.S. \par \par \uc2  economic health and the prospect of further rate cuts by the \par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters expected the March jobs report \par \par \uc2  to reveal a higher unemployment rate, up to 4.3 percent from \par \par \uc2  the current 4.2 percent rate where it has been lodged all year. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  SINKS, INFLATION FEARED \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  buckled under the yen's renewed weakness, \par \par \uc2  with the Indonesian rupiah leading the losers due to persistent \par \par \uc2  corporate dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  underpinned some of the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealers said the Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the \par \par \uc2  dollar through state banks while Bank Indonesia was spotted \par \par \uc2  selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to cap the rupiah's fall at \par \par \uc2  10,930. \par \par \uc2  The move came after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was \par \par \uc2  rumoured to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Monday and the \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggested earlier this week that it had been \par \par \uc2  in the market to stave off baht volatility. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expressed concerns sustained declines in these \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could worsen the already bleak growth prospect of \par \par \uc2  the region as they increased risk of inflation. \par \par \uc2  "This stops people from placing a one-way bet on the \par \par \uc2  direction of inflation and interest rates in the region," said \par \par \uc2  David Fernandez, head of Asian sovereign research at JP Morgan \par \par \uc2  Chase. \par \par \uc2  "The market right now is taking \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness seriously \par \par \uc2  and it's time to be cautious as hopes that central banks would \par \par \uc2  continue to cut rates to boost the economy will have to be put \par \par \uc2  on pause," he said. \par \par \uc2  WEAK YEN COULD HIT PEGS \par \par \uc2  There has been concern in the market that the yen's \par \par \uc2  sustained weakness could raise the spectre of competitive \par \par \uc2  devaluation among Asian pegged \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Malaysian \par \par \uc2  ringgit, Chinese yuan and Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  The yen has depreciated by around 10 percent year this \par \par \uc2  year. While other free-floated \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  can fall in tandem \par \par \uc2  with the yen, these pegged \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have not, making them \par \par \uc2  look overvalued. \par \par \uc2  "There has been yet again rhetoric about pressure on the \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong economy via price and output adjustments witnessed in \par \par \uc2  1998, and about how the Chinese renminbi peg stands in the face \par \par \uc2  of persistent yen weakness," said Lian Chia Liang, analyst at \par \par \uc2  Merrill Lynch. \par \par \uc2  China managed to hold the yuan steady against the dollar \par \par \uc2  despite Asian financial crisis which saw the yen falling past \par \par \uc2  140 in summer 1998. Investors are questioning if the country \par \par \uc2  would be able to do the same this time. \par \par \uc2      Yan Haiwang, deputy governor of the People's Bank of China, \par \par \uc2  said on Friday that a devaluation of the yuan was impossible. \par \par \uc2      "I have never thought about devaluing the yuan and it is \par \par \uc2  quite impossible for that to happen," he told an economic forum \par \par \uc2  attended by finance and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials from Japan and \par \par \uc2  China. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0829 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.87\tab  123.98\tab    -0.71\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8158\tab  1.8065\tab    -0.51\par  Taiwan dlr     32.94\tab   32.98\tab    +0.12\par  Korean won   1342.10\tab 1347.00\tab    +0.37\par  Baht\tab      45.63\tab   45.25\tab    -0.83\par  Peso\tab      50.00\tab   50.10\tab    +0.20\par  Rupiah\tab 10850.00     10680.00\tab    -1.57\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     124.87\tab  114.45\tab    -8.34\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8158\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.37\par  Taiwan dlr     32.80\tab   32.90\tab    +0.30\par  Korean won   1342.10\tab 1277.00\tab    -4.85\par  Baht\tab      45.63\tab   43.70\tab    -4.23\par  Peso\tab      50.00\tab   50.75\tab    +1.50\par  Rupiah\tab 10850.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -12.72\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ASIAN STOCK MARKETS  0829 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Market\tab  Current\tab Prev Close     Pct Move\par  Tokyo\tab  13383.76     13381.38\tab    +0.02\par  Hong Kong   12386.61     12063.71\tab    +2.68\par  Singapore    1662.07\tab 1676.88\tab    -0.88\par  Taipei\tab  5515.13\tab 5405.85\tab    +2.02\par  Seoul\tab    506.22\tab  493.69