\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk Gov: To Ensure THB Doesn't Weaken Too Much \b0\par\par\uc2 591 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2001\par 04:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul confirmed Thursday that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the offshore market to control the baht's movement. \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol told reporters that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold "not a big amount" of dollars to slow the baht's weakening pace but not stop it. He said the move took place in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot, swap and forward markets. \par \par \uc2  He said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also adjusted its already tight \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading regulations to stem speculation against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He didn't elaborate. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed to limit the baht's volatility," he said. \par \par \uc2  The baht slid to a 37-month low of 45.50 baht to the dollar Wednesday after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials declined to confirm market speculation that an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had taken place. At 0250 GMT Thursday, it was trading at THB45.325 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to monitor the baht's movement and will take action again if necessary. \par \par \uc2  He said that Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra had also expressed his concern over the baht's weakness and wanted it to stabilize. \par \par \uc2  The government has said in the past that it's not worried by the baht's slide as it has been in line with regional weakness and would help boost slowing export growth. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak Wednesday denied that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, adding that there was no reason to worry for the baht's weakness. \par \par \uc2  But traders said there had been speculation in the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars in London trading late Tuesday after the baht hit a low of 45.45 and probably again Wednesday when it hit its new 37-month low of 45.50. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also appeared to tighten liquidity in the offshore market where implied \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap rates shot up to over 20%. \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol didn't appear concerned over the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves as the amount sold was small. He said that in the past, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had taken advantage of a stronger baht to buy dollars for debt repayment purposes, including payments to the International Monetary Fund. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  repaid $400 million to the IMF in the first quarter of 2001. Its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $32.6 billion as of March 23. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Chatu Mongol said that commercial banks should make efforts to lower their operating cost in order to reduce lending rates and narrow the wide margin between lending and deposit rates. \par \par \uc2  Banks have been maintaining a wide margin of over five percentage points to compensate for the high cost of provisioning against nonperforming loans. \par \par \uc2  "Once banks manage to lower their cost, lending rates should go down, but it's going to take time," Chatu Mongol said. \par \par \uc2  He said he would like nonperforming loans to drop to below 10% of total lending in the financial system, from 17.8% at the end of February, for commercial banks to run their business cost-effectively. \par \par \uc2  The government has initiated plans to set up a state asset management company that will buy THB1.1 trillion worth of bad debt from state-owned banks and up to THB250 billion from private sector banks. \par \par \uc2  -By Supunnabul Suwannakij and Jenny Paris, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266 0744; supunnabul suwannakij@dowjones.com, jenny.paris@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx4501giv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
