\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Stumble on weak yen, U.S.-China woes. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2001\par 10:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 4 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  buckled under a heap of negative factors, ranging from a weaker yen, U.S.-China tensions over a U.S. spy plane, and increased risk aversion towards the region as the global economy cooled on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the dollar remained a preferred \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite sustained losses in U.S. equities, a sharp decline in U.S. interest rates, and easing oil prices. \par \par \uc2  "Longer-term structural optimism for the U.S. economy triumphs for now over shorter-term cyclical pessimism with respect to the value of dollar," said a Salomon Smith Barney report. \par \par \uc2  It suggested that investors continue to stay long of dollars against the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yen retained its bearish tone after a much-hyped package of emergency measures for Japan's ailing economy was delayed. Dealers said the dollar might consolidate briefly around this level before moving higher toward 127 yen. \par \par \uc2  The standoff between Washington and Beijing over a U.S. spy plane and its crew also kept the market nervous. \par \par \uc2  China has adopted a hardline, blaming the U.S. for Sunday's mid-air collision between the spy plane and a Chinese fighter over the South China Sea, demanding an apology and holding on to the 24 crew. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar trailed off to lows of 1.8158 in quiet afternoon trade, with sporadic U.S. dollar bids countered by unwinding of long positions. \par \par \uc2  There was renewed talk of Singapore's Changi airport looking to buy Sydney Airport after the Australian government said last week it would complete the sale in the second half of 2001. The Sydney Airports Corp has said its book value is A$3.25 billion. Dealers said prospects of further capital outflows related to more M&A activities were handicapping the Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  A disappointing 1.2 point dip in Singapore's Purchasing Manager's Index in March reinforced concerns about the slowing economy, analysts said. The figure represented the second month of contraction since January 1999. \par \par \uc2  However, one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist said the downside was well supported at 1.8180 and then 1.8230, levels where she said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in London on Monday, when the Sing dollar fell to decade lows. \par \par \uc2  She said her calculation showed the Sing dollar nominal exchange rate was bobbing out of the policy band, which the MAS uses to manage the economy. \par \par \uc2  "Bears think they can pressurise the Sing forever, but stop and think about it. This is way out of the band," she said. \par \par \uc2  "I think the MAS is waiting for a big jump (in dollar/Sing) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market again." \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won slid to a fresh 30-month closing low of 1,365.2 as the yen stumbled past 126, despite the Korean government's pledges to introduce measures aimed at stabilising the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading was initially cautious as the market remained wary over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Bank of Korea was rumoured to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  via state banks on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  However, the won later succumbed as the dollar gained more ground on the yen and foreign investors sold a net 177.4 billion won worth of stocks. \par \par \uc2  Authorities said earlier they were working on a package of measures to stabilise the market. They also repeated warnings that they were watching the market closely. \par \par \uc2  On the offshore non-deliverable forward market, one-month dollar/won was at 1,358.5/59.5 against 1,344.5/45.5 late Tuesday and the three-month was at 1,362.5/64.5 against 1,347.3/48.3. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT The baht turned tail to hit fresh three-year lows of 45.47, despite official efforts to talk it up. \par \par \uc2  Local banks joined a selling spree with banks in Singapore and foreign banks in Bangkok, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market had been wary about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  after talk circulated authorities sold U.S. dollars via a Singapore-based bank at 45.40 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But bears regained confidence in trouncing the baht after Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said the BOT had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the baht. \par \par \uc2  He said the baht's weakness was caused by external factors and it did not suggest the Thai economy was not sound. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the baht has been too volatile versus regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that it was ready to act. \par \par \uc2  "They are trying to find ways to slow the pace of the decline," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst said. "They don't mind the decline. They mind the pace of the decline." \par \par \uc2  He said firmer offshore baht funding costs provided the only solace for the baht. The one-month forward rate stood at 50/70 satang per dollar against 50/60 earlier. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah hit a three-week low of 10,600 as demand for dollars from local corporates spiked despite sporadic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said with an increase in the flow of bad news from the economic front, in addition to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness across the region, most corporates were staying long of dollars. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a European bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pumped in about $25 million and finally succeeded in defending the 10,600 mark and propping it up to 10,560. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said early \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had little impact as the bank sold dollars in small amounts, at different levels. \par \par \uc2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin said BI would continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the rupiah would get worse without the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile chief economics minister Rizal Ramli warned the 2001 budget deficit could overshoot the target of 3.2 percent of gross domestic product to slightly over five percent. \par \par \uc2  The defence minister said violence could get worse if political tensions do not ease. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso eased to a low of 50.17, not seen since mid-January, as importers chased the dollar up expecting more pressure from other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming days. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said most exporters were holding back their earnings while importers were trying to lock in their dollar needs before the peso slipped lower with the regional downturn. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.S. bank said support for the peso was likely to come in at around 50.20 while its upside was capped at 49.80. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar tripped over the weaker yen, but resisted the 33 level thanks to wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was speculated to be selling dollars when the Taiwan dollar edged to 32.995. But they added the market was expected to test that level again, especially if the yen showed further weakness. \par \par \uc2  Outflows from foreign investors also hobbled sentiment towards the local dollar as Taiwan stocks closed lower for the fourth straight session. Foreign investors sold a net T$5.132 billion in Taiwan shares on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan was also coping with anxiety over the stand-off between the U.S. and China over a U.S. surveillance plane. China regards Taiwan as a renegade province and has been perturbed by the Bush administration's more openly pro-Taiwan stance and possible U.S. arms sales to Taiwan. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0826 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     126.14\tab  125.54\tab    -0.48\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8155\tab  1.8120\tab    -0.19\par  Taiwan dlr    32.979\tab  32.900\tab    -0.24\par  Korean won   1364.30\tab 1343.00\tab    -1.56\par  Baht\tab      45.45\tab   45.20\tab    -0.55\par  Peso\tab      50.10\tab   49.70\tab    -0.80\par  Rupiah\tab 10580.00     10435.00\tab    -1.37\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     126.14\tab  114.45\tab    -9.27\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8155\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.35\par  Taiwan dlr    32.979\tab  32.900\tab    -0.24\par  Korean won   1364.30\tab 1277.00\tab    -6.40\par  Baht\tab      45.45\tab   43.70\tab    -3.85\par  Peso\tab      50.10\tab   50.75\tab    +1.30\par  Rupiah\tab 10580.00\tab 9470.00\ta