\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Hits New 37-Mo Low As  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears Ease \b0\par\par\uc2 914 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2001\par 12:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht hit a fresh 37-month low against the U.S. dollar in Asian spot trade Wednesday on continued corporate dollar buying, following an easing of concerns about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar finished at 45.465 baht, up from THB45.285 at the Asian close Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar tested THB45.50 in late afternoon trade before retreating slightly on profit-taking. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit had dropped as low as THB45.11 in London after the Asian close Tuesday, and dealers had believed it was Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  through an offshore bank. \par \par \uc2  After trading around THB45.20 to THB45.30 most of the morning, market participants returned to buy dollars again in the afternoon after contradictory statements by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and finance minister eased fears of any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Bandid Nijathavorn wouldn't comment on the reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but said the authorities stood ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the baht weakened excessively, and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was concerned about day-to-day volatility. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak, however, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and that there was no reason to worry. \par \par \uc2  "The government showed that they have no clear policy on how to protect the baht. That's why the baht resumed its downward journey again in the afternoon," a local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The current government was formed in February, and officials have yet to polish coordination of public statements with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has long-standing monetary and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies and fairly well-established ways of communicating its intentions to the market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to open between THB45.20 and THB45.60 Thursday, as profit-taking and tight liquidity in offshore \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap markets should cap the dollar's gains. \par \par \uc2  Bandid reminded markets of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to monitor and punish violations of its restrictions on the flow of baht to offshore markets, which make it too expensive for speculators to cover short-baht positions by borrowing in offshore swap markets. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar will eventually resume climbing to test THB46 level due to the combined impact of regional dollar strength, a sluggish local economy, and other negative regional and local factors. \par \par \uc2  An ongoing Constitutional Court hearing on an anti-corruption commission's indictment of Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra for failure to disclose assets heightened market uncertainties, although resolution of the case isn't expected until late this year at the earliest. \par \par \uc2  Thai government bond prices ended mostly flat Wednesday as the market waited for clearer direction in long-term yields, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Late selling in the December 2006 issue pushed the bid-offer range to 4.42%-4.37%, from a close Tuesday of 4.355%, but most issues closed flat. \par \par \uc2  The issue due December 2008 closed at a bid-offer of 4.99%-4.85%, around a last deal Tuesday of 4.88%. Wide spreads meant volume was thin. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand canceled a 1.46 billion baht ($1=THB45.161) offering Wednesday of 20-year government bonds, and accepted only 1.33 billion baht ($1=THB45.161) in bids in a THB3 billion offering of nine-year bonds. \par \par \uc2  The weighted-average accepted yield for the issue maturing April 9, 2010, was 5.26%, with a bid coverage ratio of only 2.67 times. \par \par \uc2  The accepted yield range was 5.15% to 5.32%, in line with expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would reject bids to cap the range below the 5.33% secondary market closing Tuesday of the government bond due March 2011. \par \par \uc2  Dealers had expected insurance companies to come up with sufficient bids for the 20-year issue, but based on extrapolations from the government bond yield curve, they had also expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reject bids if yields were closer to 7.5% than 7.0%. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's auction was to be the first for the 20-year issue, so the cancellation deprived the secondary market of any guidance on the extended yield curve. The issue due 2015 was bid at 6.35% late Wednesday with no offers, compared with a last deal Tuesday of 6.20%. \par \par \uc2  A dealer said the market has to decide how soon it thinks the Thai economy will recover. \par \par \uc2  "If you assume that next year the economy will begin to recover, then banks will begin to lend again and interest rates can go higher, and people should park their money in short-term instruments," he said. Higher yields mean lower prices. \par \par \uc2  "But if people think, like I do, that the economy will still be sluggish next year, then rates should stay flat, excess liquidity will remain in the market and should return to long-term bonds" for higher interest earnings, he said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market interest rates dropped on increasing liquidity, which rose due to the flow of funds into short-term markets, and retention of baht in nonresident accounts as foreign net selling continues on the Thai bourse. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market       Term                     Wednesday   Tuesday\par Interbank   Overnight/Most Active     1.3750%     1.5000%\par Repurchase  Overnight/Close           1.0000%     1.1250%\par             14-Day                    1.5000%     1.5000%\par             1-Month                   1.8750%     1.8750%\par             3-Month                   2.0000%     2.0000%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266\par 0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx4401jm0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
