\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Watch: Thailand May Opt For Weak Baht \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jenny Paris \par \uc2 1,013 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 01:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  A Dow Jones Newswires Column \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Bank of Thailand has sent a strong message to the markets with its new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions reporting requirements, signaling that it won't let the Thai baht become a speculative target. \par \par \uc2  But it stopped short of imposing stricter rules that would dry out offshore trading in tandem with Malaysia and more recently Indonesia, as many in the market had feared. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance served a double purpose, observers say: the Bank of Thailand isn't necessarily against a weaker baht but it's excessive volatility that it wants to avoid. In fact, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be even willing to tolerate a weaker exchange rate to help stimulate the economy which is showing signs of weakness following a spate of negative data. \par \par \uc2  "I would expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to show more latitude from now on in dollar/baht appreciation," Simon Flint, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at the Bank of America in Singapore, said. "There seems to be less moral outcry against people selling the baht now, than there was before." \par \par \uc2  News that Thailand drifted to a trade deficit for the first time in 11 months in January after a 3.9% drop in exports, stirred worries that the impact of the global economic slowdown on the country would be felt earlier than expected. The government has since tried to ease such fears, promptly leaking data showing that the trend won't continue into February. \par \par \uc2  But Thailand's fragile economic recovery still remains vulnerable to external risks, leading analysts to believe that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't stand in the way of a weaker baht. \par \par \uc2  Barclays Capital notes in its latest comment that the weakening Japanese yen will increase the likelihood of Asian exports contracting for the first time since early 1999. \par \par \uc2  This could be particularly felt in Thailand, where "any further softening of exports is likely to result in an extension of the current ultra-loose monetary policy, whereby real deposit rates are tending to zero," Barclays said. It added that the weak yen makes the bank's year-end target for the baht of THB48 to the dollar look conservative. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from cutting its already low 1.5% 14-day benchmark repurchase rate at its latest monetary policy board meeting earlier this month, despite fueling market expectations it might do so to stimulate growth. But it has signaled its desire to keep bond yields low by frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support bond prices that have come under pressure on increased supply. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Further Tightening Depends On Market's Response\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht has slipped from about 43 baht to the dollar since March 1 -\par when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced its new disclosure regulations - to\par THB43.60 to the dollar Tuesday, weighed by January's weak trade data and\par the recent slide of the Japanese yen and the Indonesian rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Effective March 1, the Bank of Thailand introduced detailed disclosure\par requirements on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions. Banks must reveal more\par details on their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealings such as the names of their\par customers and specify the purpose of each transaction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The new requirements were initially received with caution, briefly\par curtailing trading, but soon traders worked out ways to bypass the\par stringent rules by simply declaring trading as their main purpose of the\par transaction, a practice that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appears to allow for now.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's been about two weeks that the measures have been in effect and\par the market appears to understand them and accept them," Bandid\par Nijathaworn, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  assistant governor, told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said that a further tightening of regulations would depend on the\par market's response to the new requirements. "We'll have to give it some\par more time to be able to fully assess the response of the market," he\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The Bank of Thailand will let the baht move according to the market\par mechanisms," Anusorn Tamajai, executive vice president at Citibank in\par Thailand said. "A weaker baht is better for the economy."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Anusorn expects the baht to slide toward THB45 to the dollar over the\par next three to six months, driven mainly by regional rather than domestic\par factors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far appears comfortable with the baht's gradual\par slide and feels no need to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  senior director,\par Atchana Waiquamdee, Tuesday said that the baht has weakened on external\par factors only and has been rather stable compared to other regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We have no need to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market," she said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Domestic Risks Could Pressure The Baht\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par To be sure, the baht has been fairly resilient in recent days despite\par volatility across the region. High expectations about the new\par government's policies which is moving fast to fulfill promises to set up\par a state asset management company that will bail out banks from costly\par bad debt, have helped support the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  despite adverse market\par conditions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But market participants are still concerned that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par could opt for tighter \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulations if pressure on the\par baht mounted, as reflected in the recent spike of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap\par rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts warn that there are still risks in the domestic front that\par could test the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's tolerance levels in the months ahead. The\par new government's policies haven't been tested yet and disappointment may\par follow the initial optimism if results fall below expectations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Political uncertainty may also play a role next month when the\par Constitutional Court opens a hearing against Prime Minister Thaksin\par Shinawatra on charges of attempting to conceal his wealth. If found\par guilty, Thaksin will be banned from politics for five years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There are still domestic risk factors that could lead to a 2% to 3%\par appreciation of the dollar against the baht in coming months," Flint\par said. "But I wouldn't expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to impose stiffer\par regulations as a result of that."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Jenny Paris, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266 0744;\par jenny.paris@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1154 4253 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3e0171u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
