\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Thai govt says will not interfere in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  policy. \b0\par\par\uc2 221 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2001\par 11:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Feb 26 (Reuters) - Thai Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said on Monday the new government of Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra had no policy of interfering in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate policy. \par \par \uc2  "The exchange rate policy is just part of the overall economic policy ... and the government has no intention of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Somkid said during a parliamentary debate. \par \par \uc2  "This government will encourage the Bank of Thailand to apply its monetary policies and the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, along with government policies to achieve the national development strategies." \par \par \uc2  Somkid was responding to criticism from opposition politicians that the government's policy on the exchange rate was ambiguous. \par \par \uc2  Thaksin told parliament his government would "pursue a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy that accommodates income generation for people at all levels, that benefits overall economic recovery, and that increases competitiveness of the high-local-content manufacturing sector". \par \par \uc2  Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda, finance minister in the previous government led by Chuan Leekpai, accused the government of ignoring market mechanisms in pursuing its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  "The way the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is written makes it seem that this government would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, not giving priority to market forces," Tarrin told parliament. \par \par \uc2  The two-day government policy debate will end on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx2q05ace\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
