\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - On higher ground, but risks lurking. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2000\par 10:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 27 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  regained their footing in subdued trading late Monday, helped by Nasdaq-inspired gains in regional equities markets. \par \par \uc2  But analysts say consistently high oil prices, slowing external demand, still vulnerable technology stocks, and political turmoil continued to haunt regional markets. \par \par \uc2  A stronger Thai baht gave Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially the Singapore dollar, a leg up. The baht got a boost from lingering concerns over tight offshore baht liquidity and the approval of Thai Petrochemical Industry's debt restructuring plan. \par \par \uc2  Moves by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  which amounted to indirect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also kept the baht firm. \par \par \uc2  The bank said commercial banks would have to sell to the authorities at a discount dollars obtained from one-day non-commercial dollar/baht deals made with offshore or non-resident parties. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the yen was trying to stay above the 111 level and the euro was propped up by wariness over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht is likely to hold its ground in the near-term after the Bank of Thailand announced it would impose a penalty on banks which extended non-commercial baht credits to offshore parties beyond the limit of 50 million baht. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday commercial banks would have to sell to the authorities at a discount dollars obtained from one-day non-commercial dollar/baht deals made with non-resident parties. \par \par \uc2  It said the instruction would be effective for November 27-29. During this period, commercial banks would have to sell to the Bank of Thailand the dollars bought through such deals at a discount of 1.20 baht per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "This translates roughly into a borrowing cost of around 1,000 percent per year," said a dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Even before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made the announcement, talk of such a move had been swirling in the market all day, keeping dollar bulls at bay. \par \par \uc2  "But the baht retreated a bit at one point in the afternoon due to real commercial demand for dollars. However, I don't think the dollar will go far in the immediate term given the cost of carrying long dollar/baht positions now," said another dealer at a European bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  News of creditors approving a $3.8 billion debt-restructuring plan for the country's biggest corporate defaulter Thai Petrochemical Industry barely cheered the market as its management vowed to appeal against the vote. \par \par \uc2  The case is seen by foreign investors as a test case for Thailand's efforts to tackle its crushing bad loans burden. \par \par \uc2  One-month forward rates eased marginally to 6.0/16.0 satang per dollar offshore and -13.00/-11.50. The overnight interbank rate also nudged lower to 2.75-3.00 percent. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was buoyed by dollar remittances from Filipinos working abroad, but most investors were cautious on the eve of a Senate hearing on whether to push ahead with the impeachment trial of President Joseph Estrada or dismiss the case. \par \par \uc2  The government put thousands of troops on high alert on Monday to quash any violent protests that might take place. \par \par \uc2  "The inflows remained a key driver of the market today. But from tomorrow, politics is likely to take centrestage again," said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "Players are very cautious judging from offshore trading volumes which were fairly thin," he said. \par \par \uc2  But Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said on Monday he expected the peso to stabilise due to a growing belief the political problems would be resolved constitutionally. \par \par \uc2  The government said its external financing requirement for 2001 would total about $1.9 billion, covering an expected budget deficit of 85 billion pesos as well as other government debt servicing needs. \par \par \uc2  One-month non-deliverable forward peso was quoted at 49.80/49.95 per dollar while six-month NDFs were quoted at 52.60/53.20. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar slipped past 1.7600 in early trading, but later bounced back above that level as players took profit on the U.S. dollar's gains. \par \par \uc2  Dealers had been expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore to cap the U.S. dollar's rise at 1.76. However, the MAS was not spotted in the market on Monday, and dealers were nonchalant about any possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authority. \par \par \uc2  Dealers blamed the early weakness in the Sing dollar on the wilting yen. They later said the Sing dollar strengthened in line with the baht. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar is managed against an undisclosed trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and is vulnerable to moves in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said support for the U.S. dollar was seen at 1.7550, as there was congestion around that area during mid to late October. Resistance for the U.S. dollar was expected at 1.7620, which was the intraday high on November 24. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won managed to hold onto most of its gains, though dealers said volume was thin in the wake of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slump to a 13-month intraday low last week. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors buying some 206.7 billion won worth of shares on Monday lifted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, the won's rise was capped around 1,180, as oil importers and offshore players were buying dollars around that level. \par \par \uc2  Despite Monday's gains, analysts say the won will see further losses in the longer term due to softer economic growth, weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its main competitors Japan and Taiwan, and anxieties over government-led corporate reforms. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar barely moved from Friday's close of 32.875, ending at 32.878. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said month-end U.S. dollar selling by exporters kept the Taiwan dollar buoyed. However concerns over the island's slowing economy, the unresolved issue of increasing bad loans, and ongoing political turmoil were still damping sentiment. \par \par \uc2  As further evidence of Taiwan's economic slowdown, the top economic planning agency said the index of leading business indicators fell further in October due to the anxiety reigning in local financial markets. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market needed fresh incentives and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to continue defending the 33 level, if it came under fire again this week. \par \par \uc2  But given the dimmer economic prospects for Taiwan, analysts said the bank would have to allow more weakening in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was steady in a thin market, with trade in some local banks cut short as Muslim dealers observed the first day of the fasting month. \par \par \uc2  The unit was underpinned by the firmer baht and Singapore dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There is not much going on onshore. The rupiah moved in a narrow range and took its cue from the regionals," said a dealer at a European bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  The saga over the recapitalisation and board reshuffle at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained in focus, with players awaiting parliamentary approval of changes to laws governing the bank. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said uncertainty over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's role and leadership would only undermine the rupiah if it persisted. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0951 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     111.34\tab  110.94\tab    -0.36\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7553\tab  1.7584\tab    +0.18\par  Taiwan dlr    32.878\tab  32.875\tab    -0.01\par  Korean won   1186.00\tab 1188.00\tab    +0.17\par  Baht\tab      43.48\tab   43.77\tab    +0.67\par  Peso\tab      49.33\tab   49.25\tab    -0.16\par  Rupiah\tab  9449.00\tab 9455.00\tab    +0.06\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     111.34\tab  102.21\tab    -8.20\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7553\tab  1.6640\tab    -5.20\par  Taiwan dlr    32.878\tab  31.380\tab    -4.56\par  Korean won   1186.00\tab 1135.00\tab    -4.30\par  Baht\tab      43.48\tab   37.45\tab   -13.87\par  Peso\tab      49.33\tab   40.20\tab   -18.51\par  Rupiah\tab  9449.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -26.18\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7997\tab    +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwbr00p6s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\pic