\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk Gov: Reserves Right To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  For Baht \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2000\par 08:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - - 23/11/07-12G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0712GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  - - 23/11/07-12G \par \par \uc2  0712GMT \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul told reporters Thursday that Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the baht, but will do so as little as possible. \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol wouldn't comment on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been active recently, but Deputy Governor Pakorn Malakul Na Ayudhya said Wednesday that there has been no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the baht's recovery in recent days. \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep its tight regulations against \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements to fend off possible speculation against the baht. \par \par \uc2  "We tighten regulations every day and we'll keep monitoring the market for unusual movements," he said, without elaborating whether tighter controls were being considered. \par \par \uc2  Speaking earlier at a business luncheon, Chatu Mongol called on the next government to ensure the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence in conducting monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  He said that unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was granted full independence and reported to parliament and not the government, its ability to stabilize the economy would be restricted. \par \par \uc2  "The role of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in helping to keep the economy stable will no longer be possible soon," he warned. \par \par \uc2  He said independence wouldn't mean that monetary policy would be in contrast with the government's economic policies. \par \par \uc2  "These two policies must be intertwined," he said. \par \par \uc2  A bill on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence is pending parliamentary approval and will have to be examined by the new parliament that will emerge from general elections Jan. 6. \par \par \uc2  -By Jenny Paris and Chanyaporn Chanjaroen, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266 0744; chanyaporn.chanjaroen@dowjones.com, jenny.paris@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwbn05o17\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
