\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk Mum On Reports Of Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2000\par 05:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday declined to comment whether it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the weakening baht. \par \par \uc2  In response to Dow Jones Newswires' question on reports that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected late Wednesday, Assistant Governor Bandid Nijtavorn said: "It is the Bank of Thailand policy that we don't comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a daily basis. We also never comment on our \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The Bangkok Post, a Thai daily, Thursday reported there has been market speculation of "heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which might have been behind the baht's significant rebound against the dollar in late trading Wednesday after the local market closed. \par \par \uc2  The baht hit a high at THB43.35 to the dollar in New York overnight, compared with THB43.78 at the Asian close Wednesday. It was a sharp recovery from a 32-month low at THB44.34 to the dollar reached Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht's sudden rebound was due to an offshore baht liquidity squeeze, which pushed offshore swap premiums higher, thus making it costlier to hold the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Bandid noted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains its current regulations on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, and refused to say whether it planned to tighten its regulations further or ban offshore baht trading, as reported in the Bangkok Post. \par \par \uc2  Effective Nov. 1, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has required investors to submit detailed information on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Chanyaporn Chanjaroen, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744;\par chanyaporn.chanjaroen@dowjones.com\par -0- 23/11/00 04-19G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwbn05nuh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
