\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals drift within weak ranges. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,171 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2000\par 12:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 25 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a mixed \par \par \uc2  bag late on Wednesday, mostly holding their ground within \par \par \uc2  recent weak trading ranges. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Korea and \par \par \uc2  a holiday in Indonesia and an off-day in Singapore on Thursday \par \par \uc2  kept activity and movement in the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  markets subdued. \par \par \uc2  But the peso plumbed a new all-time low as the political \par \par \uc2  turmoil amid impeachment proceedings against President Joseph \par \par \uc2  Estrada kept sentiment bearish. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said lingering worries about U.S. tech stocks, an \par \par \uc2  expected slow down in global growth and high oil prices were \par \par \uc2  likely to keep regionals under pressure. \par \par \uc2  "Even if there is a soft landing in the U.S. and the Fed \par \par \uc2  keeps interest rates unchanged till the end of the year, there \par \par \uc2  will be problems," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  He said global growth was likely to peak, Japan's growth \par \par \uc2  was likely to remain positive but weak and Europe was likely to \par \par \uc2  raise interest rates to stem inflation and defend the euro. \par \par \uc2      He said oil prices would eventually come down but not \par \par \uc2  before the middle of next year. \par \par \uc2      "The scenario represents a bearish outlook for growth and \par \par \uc2  exports and further easing of most of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \par \par \uc2  region," he said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro\tab   fell to a record low against the dollar as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market overcame its fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the absence\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par supportive statements from the Group of 20 meeting in Canada.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen slipped after a firm Tokyo start on a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par statement from U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reiterating long-standing U.S. support for a strong dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Oil prices were firmly entrenched above $33 a barrel as key\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. oil data increased the fear of a crunch in winter heating\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par oil supplies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht see-sawed as the market was caught in a tug of war\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between Bangkok-based players taking profit on the dollar's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent gains and Singapore-based dealers squaring their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions before a holiday on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A dealer at a local bank in Singapore said there was heavy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar-selling at the beginning of the session, but that turned\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around when the dollar was deemed as being oversold. "We still\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prefer to go long on dollars," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Bangkok said the market generally ignored\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par comments by the Thai Prime Minister Chuan Leekpai and local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks were spotted taking profit on the dollar around 43.70.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The prime minister told Reuters earlier the level of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht should be determined by the market. Separately, he said he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wasn't too concerned with the recent baht weakness and still\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected strong exports growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      Analysts say the economy may actually benefit from a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weaker baht as it is a boon for exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     While the dollar has been finding it difficult to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par convincingly break the 44 baht level - a technically\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par significant level - many analysts and dealers expect it to hit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 44.50 in the next month. Investors view the baht as a proxy for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the less liquid rupiah and peso. Moreover, the low interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates in Thailand make the baht an attractive funding play for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah barely budged as markets in Jakarta were closed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par due to a public holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Given Indonesia's changeable politics, local companies have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been dominating that market, as offshore players with little\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appetite for risk continue to avoid it.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volumes in both the offshore and onshore markets have been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par razor-thin and with little bullish news coming out of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia, most analysts forecast further downside for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso slipped to a record low of 49.80 to the dollar as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par political uncertainty surrounding the impeachment proceedings\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against Estrada kept sentiments bearish.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor, Rafael Buenaventura, confirmed the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but he declined to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par provide details.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  started selling dollars soon\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after the peso slipped in early trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst said Buenaventura's statement on Tuesday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did not plan a rate hike for now could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par have contributed to the early fall.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab    -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won traded within a tight range in thin trading on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par back of remarks by Finance Minister Jin Nyum that the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government would limit the downside of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers said the impact of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's verbal\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to smooth the won's slide would not work for long.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said worries about the Nasdaq coming off, fears of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par escalation in the Middle East tension pushing up oil prices and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the outflow of foreign funds from equities was likely to hamper\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the recovery of the won.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The benchmark KOSPI\tab    closed 0.50 percent lower at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 542.33.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar was softer against the dollar, as the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  found favour in the spot and non deliverable\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forward (NDF) market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Mohktar Hassan, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at research house IFR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian Eye said the Taiwan dollar's trading trend has been to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par open strong and end soft against the dollar with opening levels\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par supported by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  selling of dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A 1.78-percent rise in the key Taiwan stock index on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday did little to support the Taiwan dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Instead, active buying of the U.S. dollar in the NDF market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and demand for the U.S. dollar for debt repayments pushed the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan dollar lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht stole the limelight away from the Singapore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, which shuffled along a narrow range in quiet trading,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A dealer at a European bank noted that activity only picked\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par up in the afternoon, when London-based players bought U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars around S$1.7525/30.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar has followed regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the past few sessions, hurt by regional sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Moreover, the Sing dollar is managed in a trade-weighted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par basket so it is affected by weakness in the euro and yen, which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par carry greater weightage in that basket.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers also said weakness in the euro would drag down the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sing dollar in overnight trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     108.10\tab  108.10\tab    +0.00\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7543\tab  1.7510\tab    -0.19\par  Taiwan dlr    32.072\tab  32.048\tab    -0.07\par  Korean won   1137.00\tab 1137.00\tab    +0.00\par  Baht\tab      43.73\tab   43.79\tab    +0.14\par  Peso\tab      49.62\tab   49.20\tab    -0.85\par  Rupiah\tab  8965.00\tab 8950.00\tab    -0.17\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     108.10\tab  102.21\tab    -5.45\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7543\tab  1.6640\tab    -5.15\par  Taiwan dlr    32.072\tab  31.380\tab    -2.16\par  Korean won   1137.00\tab 1135.00\tab    -0.18\par  Baht\tab      43.73\tab   37.45\tab   -14.36\par  Peso\tab      49.62\tab   40.20\tab   -18.98\par  Rupiah\tab  8965.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -22.20\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.8000\tab    +0.01.