\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht defies  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2 , heads down further. \b0\par\par\uc2 456 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2000\par 13:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  *** Reuters is planning to centralise some of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reporting in Southeast Asia. \par \par \uc2  The following report will be included in a longer regional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  item from October 30. \par \par \uc2  If you have any questions please call Sonali Desai on Reuters Asia Treasury Desk +65-870-3090.*** \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Oct 20 (Reuters) - The Thai baht erased early gains and resumed its downward momentum in late Asian trade on Friday due to dollar demand from corporates and offshore parties amid the uncertainty over the Thai economic and political outlook. \par \par \uc2  Comments by \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor about a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market gave short-term support to the baht, leading it up as high as 43.26 per dollar midday. \par \par \uc2  But by 1110 GMT, the baht was trading at 43.67/72 per dollar compared with 43.31/36 in early Asian trade. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand Governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul said his bank was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the exchange rate became too volatile. He said part of the reason for recent falls in the baht was speculation against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Corporates were very active in afternoon trade while offshore parties were back to buy dollars after unwinding some positions after the (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) comments," said a dealer at a major local bank. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers reported a market rumour that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by buying baht at 43.40 but most dealers shared the view that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not yet entered the market. \par \par \uc2  "I didn't see any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," said a dealer at a European bank. He added that the recent rebound was due to dollar stop-loss orders linked to an expiry on Thursday of dollar/baht options. \par \par \uc2  "There were some dollar sales left over from Thursday. After the options expired, there was no reason to hold dollars," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  They said a foreign entity had previously hedged against investment in Thailand by buying a call option to buy dollars and sell baht at a strike price of 44 baht per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was more cautious about trading after the verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and before a long three-day weekend holiday in Thailand. \par \par \uc2  Thai financial markets will be closed on Monday for Chulalongkorn Day and will reopen on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  One-month dollar/baht offshore forwards rose to -6.0/-3.0 satang/dollar early versus -8.0/-5.0 in early trade. Onshore forwards were up slightly to -15.50/-14.50 satang/dollar versus -16.00/-15.00. \par \par \uc2  One-day interbank rates were at 1.75-2.00 percent late versus 1.75-1.875 percent early. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwak03u6f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
