\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk Monetary News Conference Delayed To 1000 GMT \b0\par\par\uc2 220 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2000\par 08:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday it will delay a news conference scheduled to follow a monetary policy board meeting to 1000 GMT (6:00 a.m. EDT), after the close of local markets, to avoid any unnecessary impact on intraday prices. \par \par \uc2  The news conference was originally scheduled for early afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect no immediate change in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's low interest rate policy - which is reflected by the 1.5% 14-day repurchase market rate. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  reaffirmed its commitment to keeping rates low by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the secondary bond market to drive the government bond yield curve lower. \par \par \uc2  The monetary policy board's forecast ranges for inflation are expected to rise, however, due to weakness in the baht \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and high oil prices. \par \par \uc2  Officials didn't give details of the meeting's results, saying only that they wanted to avoid any impact on markets. \par \par \uc2  Only general indications of the policy meeting's results are expected later Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The new quarterly Inflation Report, containing a full range of forecasts under various scenarios and slated for approval at Tuesday's meeting, is to be released in full Oct. 24. \par \par \uc2  -By Chanyaporn Chanjaroen, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; chanyaporn.chanjaroen@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwah0519c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
