\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk Tightens Its Grip As Baht Hits New Lows \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jenny Paris \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 720 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2000\par 13:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stood idle through most of the baht's woes in recent months, at times even encouraging its slippery ride. \par \par \uc2  But as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to hit fresh lows, exceeding even the most bearish estimates, the Bank of Thailand appears to tighten its grip for the first time, indicating it is ready to step in and defend the baht. \par \par \uc2  Soon after the baht hit a 28-month low of 43.68 baht to the dollar early Friday, assistant governor Chetthavee Charoenpitaks acknowledged for the first time there could be some speculative activity in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Chetthavee declined to comment whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market but did indicate that THB42 to the dollar was a fair value for the baht. He said that at THB43.00 to the dollar "the baht was too weak". \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the ability to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it should if volatility continues," said Anusorn Tamajai, economist at Citibank in Bangkok. "For now, the baht's weakness may be still acceptable as other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are also weak, but if the baht goes beyond THB44 to the dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should act." \par \par \uc2  Anusorn said that beyond that level, the baht would trigger serious inflationary pressure. \par \par \uc2  However, Supavud Saicheua, economist at Merrill Lynch, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could do little other than "just talk up the baht". \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has began in effect but they won't do anything drastic as long as uncertainties both domestically and in the region continue," Supavud said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at THB43.55 late Friday as a political turmoil in the Philippines coupled with tension in the Middle East and rising oil prices. \par \par \uc2  Chetthavee said the baht shouldn't be linked with the peso since the two countries differed " both politically and economically." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Active \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Unlikely For Now\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But much of the baht's weakness has little to do with regional\par concerns. It is rather political uncertainty at home over general\par elections expected by early January and the impact of a fresh surge in\par oil prices on Thailand's fragile economic recovery that have sustained\par pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Oil prices will definitely slow down economic activity, probably even\par more than we anticipated, while elections keep investors on a\par wait-and-see stance," Anusorn said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Citibank already revised its 2000 gross domestic product growth\par forecast to 4.2% from 4.5% previously.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Anusorn warned that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should find other ways to support\par the baht than raise interest rates, a move that would dampen growth\par further.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Among possible actions would be either to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, or tighten controls for short-term speculative\par capital and non-resident baht accounts, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised rates 400 basis points and the\par peso continued to slide," Anusorn said, referring to the Banko Sentral\par ng Pilipinas' move Thursday to hike rates after the peso hit an all-time\par low of PHP48.50 to the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of Thailand has been reluctant so far to either raise rates\par or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves\par stand at a healthy US$32.1 billion but may not be sufficient if the baht\par continues to weaken.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  apparently wants to avoid a repeat of the futile\par attempt to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the 1997 financial crisis when it\par depleted its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, but did not prevent a sharp\par devaluation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For now, it has been limited to verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and stricter\par regulations for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements. In a circular to commercial\par banks, publicized Friday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it will seek more\par information on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions, effective November 1.\par Banks will have to provide detailed information on the purpose of the\par transactions and the type of business they concern.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Any attempt to actively support the baht would be futile," Merrill\par Lynch's Supavud said. "There is no sense to do something when\par uncertainties will remain unresolved even after they take action.\par They'll just continue to talk up the baht."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Jenny Paris, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266 0744;\par jenny.paris@dowjones.com\par -0- 13/10/00 11-16G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwad04zlh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
