\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Down On Middle East Fears, Global Dlr Gains \b0\par\par\uc2 837 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2000\par 12:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht ended sharply lower against the dollar Friday on the dollar's surge against regional and global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as renewed turmoil in the Middle East shattered hopes of an easing in oil prices, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 43.575 baht, up from THB43.29 at the Asian close Thursday, but off a 28-month high of THB43.70, they said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose early on news of Thursday's events in the Middle East and fears that violence there could disrupt global oil supplies. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell back to a low of THB43.37 around midday, however, on news that Thailand should be able to sell two more nationalized banks and after comments by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official raised the prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the baht. \par \par \uc2  But a sell-off in government bonds and renewed weakness in global markets pushed the dollar higher again in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Chetthavee Charoenpitaks, assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, said there are signs of speculation against the baht in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a long-standing policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to damp volatility or to raise funding costs for speculators. \par \par \uc2  Chetthavee declined to comment on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the baht. \par \par \uc2  After the close of Bangkok markets, however, the new Bank of Thailand spokesman, Bandid Nijathaworn, said there have been no unusual movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The baht has weakened due to concerns about the strength of the domestic economy and to the regional strength of the dollar, he said. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will step up monitoring of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by requiring new forms supplying additional information on each transaction effective Nov. 1. \par \par \uc2  Analysts don't expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to waste its reserves fighting the market, but the authorities may look for ways to raise funding costs by tightening liquidity offshore, without affecting a domestic low-interest rate policy. Low domestic rates are viewed as essential to support economic recovery, debt restructuring, bank earnings and recapitalization. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is expected to rise to the THB44 to THB45 range amid political uncertainty ahead of general elections, expected between mid-December and early January, but the country's finances are in good shape, and there are no concerns about a recurrence of the 1997 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the finance ministry said HSBC Holdings Ltd. of the U.K. has agreed to terms for the sale of 75% stake in the nationalized Bangkok Metropolitan Bank. The deal should be approved by Cabinet Oct. 17. \par \par \uc2  A Thai group of businesses has also made a new offer for Siam City Bank PCL, and a similar deal should be arranged within two months. \par \par \uc2  The sales will be positive for the baht, but the good news was overwhelmed by negative sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Government bond prices plummeted Friday on oil prices, baht weakness and mutual fund selling to cover redemptions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A lack of bids and wide spreads between bids and offers pushed cash trading volume in government, state enterprise and corporate bonds down to about THB3.5 billion, from THB5.45 billion Thursday, dealers estimated. \par \par \uc2  Most yields closed 20-to-45 basis points higher. \par \par \uc2  The issue due 2011 closed Friday at 6.35%, up from 6.10% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  At the end of the session, the bid-offer spread for the issue due 2007 was 5.20%-5.13%, compared with its last yield of 4.87% Thursday. The closing spread on the 2008 issue was 5.68%-5.55%, compared with a last deal of 5.39%. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said selling is expected to continue next week as mutual funds are forced to cover redemptions. \par \par \uc2  Some selling was also seen in corporate bonds, as investors took profit to offset capital gains losses in more-liquid government bonds. \par \par \uc2  In onshore money markets, short-term rates closed mostly higher as baht weakness pushed implied yields in swap markets higher, but all rates ended off highs. \par \par \uc2  The overnight interbank interest rate ended flat at 2.25%, off a high of 2.75%. The overnight repurchase market rate ended higher at 1.75%, up from 1.25% Thursday, but off a high of 2.0%. The implied onshore tomorrow-next swap rate ended at 2.75%-3.00%, up from 2.50% Thursday but off a high of 3.50%. \par \par \uc2  Longer term money market rates were unchanged as Bank of Thailand maintained onshore liquidity to maintain its 14-day repurchase market policy-signal rate at 1.5%. \par \par \uc2  Implied swap yields rose about 10 basis points along the curve up to the one year term. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market     Term                  Friday         Thursday\par Interbank  Overnight/Most active 2.2500%        2.2500%\par Repurchase Overnight/Close       1.7500%        1.2500%\par            14-Day                1.5000%        1.5000%\par            3-Month               2.4375%        2.4375%\par -By Tom Fox; Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com\par -0- 13/10/00 10-58G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwad04zin\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
