\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht down, pressured by corporate dlr demand. \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2000\par 13:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Sept 25 (Reuters) - The Thai baht came under pressure again in late Asian trade on Monday due to persistent dollar demand from corporates for debt repayment, but was still managing to hold above last week's 27-month lows. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht's downside was limited as the market remained cautious about any possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even though the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeated it would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  faced sharp volatility. \par \par \uc2  Assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chetthavee Charoenpitaks said the baht's early gains could be attributed to the appreciation of the euro and a decision by the United States to draw on its national oil reserves. \par \par \uc2  Having hit a day high of 42.45 earlier on offshore dollar profit-taking, the baht was quoted at 42.65/70 to dollar at 1050 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "After an early rebound, corporates are bidding for dollars at every level. This is real demand as some companies are due to repay their foreign debt ahead of the end of the accounting year this month," said a dealer at major local bank. \par \par \uc2  Assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Thirachai Phuvanat naranubala said the bank's easy monetary policy had not hurt domestic consumer spending or triggered unusual capital outflows. \par \par \uc2  Despite mounting pressure to reconsider its low interest rate policy, Thirachai said state-owned banks would be asked to play a leading role in cutting loan rates to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of lower lending rates. \par \par \uc2  Baht offshore liquidity improved, indicating further upside for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  One-month dollar/baht offshore forwards eased to -7.0/-4.5 satang/dollar late versus -6.0/-4.0 in early trade and onshore forwards were little changed at -14.0/-13.5 satang/dollar. \par \par \uc2  One-day interbank rates were steady at 2.0-2.25 percent late while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-day repo rate closed at 1.2500 percent compared with 1.3750 percent in the morning. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9p06phb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
