\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht steady, offshore liquidity eases. \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2000\par 05:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Sept 20 (Reuters) - The Thai baht was steady in early Asian trade on Wednesday, with some dollar profit-taking balanced by corporate dollar demand for debt repayment, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar profit-taking by offshore players helped the baht recover to 42.16 to the dollar, but it then slipped to 42.25/28 at 0345 GMT versus 42.22/26 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Offshore players have unloaded long dollar positions to take profits since early in the morning, but the baht upside remained capped because there are a lot of dollar bids from corporates at 42.18-20," said a dealer at state-owned bank. \par \par \uc2  Recent high funding costs for borrowing baht in offshore markets had prompted offshore parties to slow their bids for dollars, but dealers expected dollar bidding interest to resume amid signs that offshore baht liquidity was easing. \par \par \uc2  Easing liquidity was reflected by a decline in short-term swap rates with one-month dollar/baht offshore forwards back to a discount of -1.0/+3.0 satang/dollar early from +3.0/+6.0 in late trade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the outlook for the baht remained bearish and they expected an attempt to test the downside, with next support at 42.50. \par \par \uc2  Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul said on Tuesday the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not about to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the Thai baht and would only do so if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turned volatile and hurt exports. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be forced to act if the the baht slipped further and approached 43 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Onshore liquidity remained flush with one-month onshore forwards slightly down to -15.25/-14.25 satang/dollar versus -15.00/-14.00 late. \par \par \uc2  One-day interbank rates were steady at 2.25-2.50 percent and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-day repo rate was quoted at 1.7500 percent at the opening. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9k0746i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
