\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Asia:Thai Baht Gets No Support In Slippery Road Ahead \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jenny Paris \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 785 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2000\par 07:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht has hit a fresh bout of weakness in recent days as worries over high oil prices peak and many analysts anticipate a further downside ahead as little support is offered from authorities. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's high exposure in oil prices and growing uncertainty over the coming general elections have been behind the latest move that led the baht to a fresh 25-month low early Tuesday of 42.33 baht to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's strength and the markets' risk aversion as they are looking to hedge against a further rise in oil prices have taken their toll on most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the baht appears to have taken the worst beating recently, outweighing even such turbulent peers as Indonesia's rupiah and the Philippine peso. \par \par \uc2  "The market is now betting that the baht will continue to weaken and could soon break the next support level which is at THB42.50," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Most analysts see the dollar around THB42 to THB43 by year end, although some expect the dollar to break the THB43 level as early as next week. Dollar buying by local importers for debt repayment and position squaring by Japanese players at the end of their six-month accounting period at the end of September will be the trigger, traders said. \par \par \uc2  But analysts feel it's more "than just the external debt story" behind the baht's weakness." \par \par \uc2  A number of factors are working against the embattled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Thailand's economy has a large exposure in oil prices, the baht's interest rate differential to the dollar is larger than in the rest of the region and signals over the outcome of upcoming general elections haven't been positive so far. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's offshore liquidity also offers scope for speculation. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Markets Puzzled By Authorities Stance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Authorities have done little to help the baht recover, often appearing\par to encourage its weakness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been giving out conflicting signals as to what\par its intentions are," Mohi-uddin said. "The markets look to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for direction and get confusion."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has so far refrained from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par indicating it's comfortable with the current baht levels. However,\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul recently gave his first hint\par that action might be on the cards, saying that "the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserved the right to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government has been equally puzzling. Days after saying that the\par "baht's weakness was a concern" that needed to be discussed with the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , deputy prime minister Supachai Panitchpakdi changed his\par tune. He said Tuesday that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was unnecessary as the baht\par shouldn't be stronger than its regional peers. He said the weak baht\par would benefit exports, still the country's main engine for economic\par growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, the market believes that authorities would be uncomfortable\par with the baht around THB42.50 to the dollar which could prove a\par significant psychological barrier.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I don't expect the dollar to go easily past THB42.50 in the short\par term," said Mark Boyne, Treasurer at Hongkong and Shanghai Banking Corp.\par in Bangkok.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Boyne said that elections will determine the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's course in the\par longer run but refused to speculate on the baht's levels after the vote\par takes place, probably late this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It will depend not only on the election outcome, but also how\par smoothly the election process will go," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Barclays Capital believes that its year-end target of THB43 to the\par dollar might be overshot and is looking for the dollar to soar to THB48\par in 2001 as high oil prices will start trimming economic growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market shrugged off better-than-expected gross domestic product\par data for the second quarter released Monday as GDP growth is still\par expected to slow in the second half of the year due to the oil prices\par and the elections, making the government's 5% target optimistic.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Thailand is vulnerable to higher oil prices... and political risk is\par growing ahead of general elections," Barclays said in its latest report.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It said that with the opposition Thai Rak Thai party looking more and\par more certain to win the vote, fiscal loosening seems unavoidable. The\par new government could also find itself at odds with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par should it want to increase a maximum 3.5% core inflation target, as Thai\par Rak Thai has indicated.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Either way, the election period is baht-negative," Barclays said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Jenny Paris, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266 0744;\par jenny.paris@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4258 5095 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9j04lu6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
