\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends At 25-Month Low On Regional Woes \b0\par\par\uc2 692 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2000\par 12:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht finished at a new 25-month low Monday as the dollar climbed against regional and global emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Local importers and debtors joined offshore speculators in buying dollars, pushing the greenback past psychological resistance of 42 baht to finish at THB42.22, up from THB41.90 at Friday's Asian close. \par \par \uc2  News of higher-than-expected second-quarter gross domestic product growth of 6.6% on year, well above a consensus forecast of 5.5%, had no effect on the market amid the overwhelmingly negative sentiment in regional markets. \par \par \uc2  Bank of America said in a daily note that it expects the dollar to hit THB42.50 in the near term. \par \par \uc2  But a foreign bank dealer said heavy local dollar buying over the last two weeks is beginning to effect short-term interest rates and liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Unless there are major moves in other regional markets, therefore, the dollar should be capped at THB42.30 on Tuesday, he said, with support at THB42.00. \par \par \uc2  Deputy Premier Supachai Panitchpakdi said Monday that baht weakness is cyclical rather than structural, due to U.S. dollar strength and Thai foreign debt repayment. \par \par \uc2  Many research houses agree, forecasting a recovery in the baht next year after hitting a low later this year of THB43 or THB44, when investment inflows return after a new government is formed following elections expected late this year. \par \par \uc2  The National Economic & Social Development Board, or NESDB, which released the GDP data, said it believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar reaches THB43. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday it reserves the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but saw no need as of last week's levels. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, short-term money market interest rates rose due to heavy local dollar buying, but only slightly, given generally flush liquidity. \par \par \uc2  The overnight repurchase market interest fell off highs in the afternoon session, reportedly on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Implied interest rates in the onshore swap market rose for terms of up to three months, but longer terms were inactive. \par \par \uc2  Several commercial banks joined a continuing round of interest rate cuts, in line with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  calls for lower lending rates. \par \par \uc2  But Supachai warned that low deposit rates were hurting domestic consumption. Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda said economic ministers would consider the commercial bank interest rate spread and several related issues next week. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market     Term                     Monday    Friday\par interbank  overnight/most active  2.25-2.50%  2.0000%\par repurchase overnight/close           1.2500%  1.1250%\par            14-day                    1.5000%  1.5000%\par            3-month                   2.4375%  2.4375%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Government bonds prices ended lower on profit-taking, after rising in\par early trade following \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  orders to buy 11-year bonds in an\par effort to flatten the yield curve, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Most yields on bonds of terms from four-to-eight years ended\par two-to-three basis points higher due to profit-taking on earlier gains,\par and on uncertainty about the effects of oil prices and a weak baht on\par long-term inflation prospects.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The 11-year issue finished Monday near the previous close of 6.28%,\par after firming to 6.23% for a brief period early Monday. Yields move in\par opposite directions to prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The six-year bond lost the most ground, as the yield ended\par three-to-four basis points higher than Friday's close of 4.76%, dealers\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Commercial bank interest rate cuts and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy tend to\par push bond yields lower, so the current trend to higher yields isn't\par expected to carry on too long or too far, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Tuesday, auctions of THB2.5 billion in government-guaranteed state\par enterprise bonds are expected result in premiums of 25-to-35 basis\par points above the government bond yield curve.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The auctions are of THB1 billion worth of nine-year bonds to be issued\par by the State Railway of Thailand, or SRT, and THB1.5 billion of 10-year\par bonds by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, or PWA.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9i04j8j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
