\par\par \b \uc2  WEEK AHEAD-Bearish baht, Nasdaq woes bode ill for Thai stocks. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Umesh Pandey \par \uc2 683 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 2000\par 04:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      BANGKOK, July 30 (Reuters) - Thai stocks hobbling along at \par \par \uc2  21-month lows can expect little help from the country's \par \par \uc2  battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week, especially after the Nasdaq's \par \par \uc2  recent losses, analysts said. \par \par \uc2      Baht bearishness returned on Friday, driving the unit \par \par \uc2  towards fresh 10-month lows of around 41.40 to the dollar after \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market only in \par \par \uc2  cases of excessive volatility. \par \par \uc2      "The policy of the Bank of Thailand since we started the \par \par \uc2  float is to leave the exchange rate to the market to \par \par \uc2  determine," said Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Tanya \par \par \uc2  Sirivedhin. \par \par \uc2      "We would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless there were signs that there \par \par \uc2  is really some excessive volatility taking place," she said on \par \par \uc2  the margins of a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conference in Singapore. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers took that, and other recent official \par \par \uc2  comments, as signs the government favoured a softer baht and \par \par \uc2  low interest-rates to help boost Thailand's export-led \par \par \uc2  recovery. \par \par \uc2      That spelt bad news for equities, with foreign investors \par \par \uc2  seen likely to withdraw yet more money from the Thai market to \par \par \uc2  protect the hard-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  value of portfolios, analysts said. \par \par \uc2      SOME IMPACT LIKELY FROM NASDAQ \par \par \uc2      Added to this, some analysts said investors were likely to \par \par \uc2  sell high-tech stocks after the technology-packed Nasdaq \par \par \uc2  composite index plunged 4.66 percent on Friday to 3,663, as \par \par \uc2  news of strong U.S. economic growth raised the odds of interest \par \par \uc2  rate increases. For the week, the Nasdaq fell 10.5 percent. \par \par \uc2      "The sharp fall in Nasdaq will impact our market, there \par \par \uc2  could be some selling in high-tech and telecoms stocks," said \par \par \uc2  Thanawat Patchimkul, strategist for DBS Thai Danu Securities. \par \par \uc2      "The impact would be more of sentiment driven rather than \par \par \uc2  anything direct," he added. \par \par \uc2      The benchmark composite SET index ended Friday down 2.62 \par \par \uc2  points or 0.89 percent at 291.60, marking a loss of 4.6 percent \par \par \uc2  on the week. The index has fallen sharply from a year high of \par \par \uc2  499.52. \par \par \uc2      Friday turnover was a tiny 1.5 billion baht ($36.4 million) \par \par \uc2  with the index in territory last seen in October 1998. \par \par \uc2      "On the technical side the market is also heading down and \par \par \uc2  therefore we have put a zero weighting on the Thai market along \par \par \uc2  with Indonesia and Philippines," said Kenneth Ng, head of \par \par \uc2  research at ING Barings Securities. \par \par \uc2  Ng said the zero weighting in ING's regional portfolio was \par \par \uc2  because Thailand's macro-economic fundamentals were not too \par \par \uc2  good, causing the house to cut its forecast for gross domestic \par \par \uc2  product growth to 5.5 percent from 5.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  FOREIGN FUNDS PULL OUT \par \par \uc2  "I see the market drifting (this) week as funds continue to \par \par \uc2  pull out," Ng added. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors have sold a net 29.67 billion baht of \par \par \uc2  stocks so far this year against 3.13 billion for the whole of \par \par \uc2  1999. \par \par \uc2      Those same investors sold a net 705 million baht last week \par \par \uc2  against 679 million for the week ending July 21. \par \par \uc2      SET's breach of key psychological support of 300 points \par \par \uc2  last week had dealers talking of further falls ahead. \par \par \uc2      They put the next support at 270 with resistance at 300 and \par \par \uc2  then 305. \par \par \uc2      "The market trend is damp and I expect the market to slide \par \par \uc2  further, with the next rebound at around 270 points," said \par \par \uc2  Aekpittaya Lemkongaek, technical analyst at Capital Nomura \par \par \uc2  Securities. \par \par \uc2  Technically, the Thai market is trading in oversold \par \par \uc2  territory with the 14-day relative strength index of the \par \par \uc2  composite index standing at 14. An RSI under 30 is usually \par \par \uc2  considered a sign the market is oversold. \par \par \uc2  Market watchers said economic data due on Monday was \par \par \uc2  unlikely to have much impact although it might highlight the \par \par \uc2  overall trend for economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "The economic data will show that the recovery of the Thai \par \par \uc2  economy is not in jeopardy," said David Loomis, head of \par \par \uc2  research at Nava Vickers Ballas Securities. \par \par \uc2  He said the market was being dragged lower by worries about \par \par \uc2  non-performing loans in the financial sector and the baht's \par \par \uc2  fall. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw7u00xvl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
