\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht weak, c.bank buying report doubted. \b0\par\par\uc2 433 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2000\par 05:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 28 (Reuters) - The Thai baht erased the previous day's recovery in early Asian trade on Friday, testing 41.20 as dealers poured cold water on a newspaper report of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The baht traded at 41.11/41.16 per dollar at 0320 GMT, down from 40.94/40.99 late on Thursday, with dealers reporting a resumption of offshore dollar buying. \par \par \uc2  The baht has fallen from near 40 to the dollar in a little over a week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were generally sceptical of a local newspaper report saying the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in London's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market late on Wednesday to support the rapidly depreciating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Most dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite The Nation's report of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying as the unit hit a 10-month low of 41.36. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market as we did not see any irregular volume," said a dealer at major state bank. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said: "There has been no sign of speculative trading in the market. The transactions are mostly from real demand from importers and exporters. I don't think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will use foreign reserves to do such things". \par \par \uc2  However, Standard and Poor's MMS in Singapore said in its report there was market talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold modest amounts of dollars at that level on Wednesday via a bank out of Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "The rumour has prompted most players be more cautious and help slow down the downtrend of the baht to 42," said another dealer at major local bank. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials were not immediately available for comment. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said exporters were holding off their dollar liquidation due to anticipation that the unit might fall further. \par \par \uc2  Increasing the chances of the baht hitting 42 was market thinking the Thai government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  preferred a weaker baht to help boost exports and economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  But some dealers said they expected short-term support at 41.20. \par \par \uc2  One-month dollar/baht offshore forwards eased slightly to -6.0/-4.0 satang/dollar versus -5.0/-4.0 late on while onshore forwards were unchanged at -12.50/-11.50 satang/dollar. \par \par \uc2  One-day interbank rates were steady at 2.0 percent and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-day repo rate was at 1.25 percent early compared with 1.0 percent late. \par \par \uc2  ((Kettiya Jittapong, Bangkok Newsroom 66 2 6375500 ext 418 \par \par \uc2  email: bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw7s00z7g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
