\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk: Baht Down On Strong Dlr; No Abnormal Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2000\par 08:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterated Tuesday that the baht's fall to new nine-month lows is caused mainly by the U.S. dollar's rise against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that it hasn't seen any unreasonably speculative or abnormal activity in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Deputy Governor Pakorn Malakul Na Ayudhya told reporters that the baht's losses are also partly due to private sector repayment of foreign debt, which is normal at a time when the cost of funds in the domestic market is lower than in overseas markets. \par \par \uc2  Pakorn's comment that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't found any abnormal or speculative trade indicates that Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said offshore trade in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot market Tuesday may be largely speculative, but that there is no evidence in swap and forward markets of rising demand for baht to leverage the ability to set up speculative long-dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  Implied interest rates in offshore and onshore swap markets are flat to lower, they said. \par \par \uc2  At 0548 GMT (1:48 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at 40.90 baht, up sharply from THB40.77 at the Asian close Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect an advance to THB41 Tuesday or Wednesday and possibly THB41.50 next week, amid uncertainty about the continuity of economic policies and reform efforts ahead of elections expected in the fourth quarter. \par \par \uc2  In support of the baht, Pakorn said the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to benefit from capital inflows for asset acquisition and investment in corporate recapitalizations. \par \par \uc2  Thailand is also running a current account surplus, although it has narrowed from a rate last year of about $1 billion a month. \par \par \uc2  Pakorn said U.S. authorities are unlikely to raise interest rates further, after hiking key rates six times. He said the effect of previous increases will take time, and there are indications that the U.S. economy is already slowing. \par \par \uc2  He didn't specify the effects expected on the Thai economy under any scenario, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has confirmed that it will maintain a low interest rate structure to support economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  -By Phisanu Phromchanya, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7p03ltj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
