\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Fin Min: Baht Weakness In Line With Yen, Regionals \b0\par\par\uc2 248 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2000\par 09:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Thai Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda said the baht \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline against the U.S. dollar Monday is line with weakness in the Japanese yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Tarrin told reporters that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  informed him there were no irregular capital flows in and out of the country, nor any abnormal speculative activity in offshore markets. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets only if there are excessive or irrational speculative flows. \par \par \uc2  Tarrin said the selling of Thai stocks was in line with losses on the U.S. Nasdaq market Friday and regional bourses Monday. \par \par \uc2  Asian markets are going through a period of adjustment to the slowdown in the U.S. economy, he said. \par \par \uc2  As the Stock Exchange of Thailand reopens for afternoon trade, the SET Index is down 10.10 points, or 3.3%, at 295.56 points. \par \par \uc2  At 0736 GMT (3:36 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at 40.715 baht, up from THB40.34 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect a temporary correction back to THB40.50 before the dollar rises to THB41, possibly this week. \par \par \uc2  Aside from regional political uncertainty and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market trends, the baht is weighed down by outflows of funds for repayment of foreign debt and political uncertainty ahead of elections expected in the fourth quarter. \par \par \uc2  -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; suttinee.yuvejwattana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7o03jw9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
