\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Baht wilts to 9-month lows on c.bank comments. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kettiya Jittapong \par \uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2000\par 13:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 12 (Reuters) - The Thai baht plumbed new nine-month lows on Wednesday as the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signalled they were prepared to tolerate a sliding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost exports and economic growth. \par \par \uc2  The embattled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered some ground in afternoon trade on offshore dollar profit-taking after it managed to avoid breaking through the 40.20 level against the dollar, and a rebound in the Philippine peso also helped. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the outlook was for further weakness. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was hit in early trade after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul said the current level of the baht was acceptable and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol said the Bank of Thailand would maintain its low interest rate policy, and added that the weak baht would be good for exporters. \par \par \uc2  By 1100 GMT, the baht was quoted at 40.03/08 to the dollar after dropping as low as 40.17 earlier. It was at its lowest levels since October 11, 1999, when it had traded at 40.30. \par \par \uc2  Deputy Prime Minister Supachai Panitchpakdi also said he was unconcerned about the baht's fall, adding that it would be beneficial for agricultural exports. \par \par \uc2  The baht breached the psychological level of 40 to the dollar on Tuesday on bearish sentiment spilling over from other regional units. The peso sank to a 30-month low on Tuesday, and the weaker tone of the rupiah also weighed on the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The baht has fallen six percent since the start of April, compared with a 21 percent decline for the rupiah and eight percent for the peso. \par \par \uc2  Supachai said he did not expect the baht to fall further because it was supported by strong economic fundamentals, and this gave the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  some support later in the day. \par \par \uc2  "There is nothing new in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy to keep interest rates low. But Suphachai's comment on the limited downside of the baht helped boost sentiment," said a dealer at major Thai bank. \par \par \uc2  DOWNSIDE RISK REMAINS \par \par \uc2  Analysts said there were fundamental domestic factors to suggest more downside risk for the baht, however, with short-term support at 40.40/50 seen as the next target. \par \par \uc2  "The baht could fall beyond our 39 baht/dollar (average) forecast for the next 12 months," Merrill Lynch Phatra Securities said in its Wednesday daily note. \par \par \uc2  The brokerage said a recent 25-basis point cut in domestic interest rates was one factor driving the unit down, as the cut would accelerate capital outflows to repay private foreign debt. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand recently said Thailand's private sector owed an extra $20 billion, raising its net debt position to $56 billion from $35 billion. \par \par \uc2  "We understand that the BOT will tolerate a baht at 41-42 before it feels that the 3.5 percent inflation target will be breached. Given the anaemic economic recovery, the chances of inflation picking up during the next 6-12 months remain small," Merrill said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw7c0a0cn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
