\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk: Baht At Appropriate Level \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2000\par 04:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul said Wednesday that recent weakness in the baht has occurred in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that it's in an appropriate range relative to its export competitors' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol told reporters on the sidelines of a seminar that there is no need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at this time. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has a policy of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  only to stem excessively\par rapid movement in exchange rates, or to make purely speculative trade\par more costly.\par - - 12/07/00 03-18G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chatu Mongol said export earnings are contributing to the emerging\par recovery in consumer spending and private investment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A low interest rate policy will be maintained to support the recovery\par in the domestic economy which is still weak, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0324 GMT (11:24 p.m. EDT Tuesday), the dollar was quoted at 40.170\par baht, up from THB40.055 early in Asian trade Wednesday, on demand from\par local importers and debtors fearing a further decline in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The next resistance is expected at THB40.30, as the U.S. dollar\par continues to climb against regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid political\par uncertainty in Indonesia, the Philippines and Thailand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Research houses are cautiously positive about Thailand's prospects,\par but investors are reluctant to move in ahead of elections and the\par formation of a new government, expected in the fourth quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744;\par suttinee.yuvejwattana@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7c03e10\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
