\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Thai baht breaks key support, hits new 9-mth low. \b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2000\par 13:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 11 (Reuters) - The Thai baht touched a new nine-month low of 40.05 to the dollar on Tuesday, hit by fresh regional weakness, but came off its lowest levels as dealers locked in some profits, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Thai Prime Minister Chuan Leekpai told reporters on Tuesday the baht's losses over the past few days did not warrant any panic, saying they were not excessive compared with declines in the Indonesian rupiah or the Philippine peso. \par \par \uc2  "I believe the baht's decline has not been larger than those in other regional countries... I think it will be allowed to find its market level," he said. \par \par \uc2  The baht rebounded to 39.99/40.04 per dollar in late Asian trade against 39.91/39.96 in the morning. In midsession it fell through the psychological level of 40 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers blamed the baht's decline on the peso, which sank to a 30-month low of 45.14 to the dollar. They said the rupiah also hovered near its 16-month low of 9,335/9,355 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The baht is tied to the peso...but I don't expect it to slide to 41 per dollar," said a dealer at a major Thai bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they did not detect any signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, the baht fell to 38.1385/38.1942 by 1103 GMT against 38.0821/38.1498 in the morning and 37.9799/38.0284 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Thai Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda said the baht had moved according to market forces and it was in line with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the government appeared willing to let the baht fall, as it wanted to keep interest rates down to boost growth. \par \par \uc2  One-month dollar/baht offshore forward stood at -1/+1 satang/dollar in late trade versus -2/0 early. Onshore swap discounts stood at -13.25/-12.25 satang/dollar against -13.00/-12.00. \par \par \uc2  The one-day interbank rate eased to 2.25-2.50 percent late from 2.50-2.75 early. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-day repurchase rate fell to 1.00 percent from 1.25 early. The 14-day repurchase rate was steady at 1.5000 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw7b01wk4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
