\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Down In Line With Rupiah,Regionals; Rates  Down \b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2000\par 12:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht ended a touch lower Thursday in line with the Indonesian rupiah, the Philippine peso and other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 39.550 baht, up marginally from THB39.545 at the Asian close Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Falling regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were the main factor behind the baht's weakness. \par \par \uc2  The baht touched a new intraday low for the year at THB39.680 early Thursday before the Bangkok opening, due in part to a false report of Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments by a news agency late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The baht regained ground in afternoon trade as offshore investors squared positions to take profit on the dollar's strength. \par \par \uc2  "There is no fresh market-moving news, so investors decided to take short-term profit before setting new positions," said a dealer at local bank. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand said late Thursday that recent weakness was in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was necessary. \par \par \uc2  The political situation in \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  did contribute to baht weakness, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said without elaboration. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's government is attempting to push electoral reforms and a budget for the fiscal year beginning Oct. 1 through Parliament before calling new elections for the lower house, probably in the fourth quarter. \par \par \uc2  Political uncertainty has largely been priced into the baht by recent weakness, but the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should slip further in the near term as investors build up long dollar positions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Internal and external factors are supporting the dollar. The baht is likely to test THB40, but not right away," said a dealer at foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  He expected the dollar to find resistance Friday at THB39.70, with support at 39.40. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, short-term rates were lower as liquidity was eased by banks' settlement of transactions initiated ahead of the half-year closing of books. \par \par \uc2  Long-term rates were unchanged. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market     Term                  Thursday       Wednesday\par Interbank  Overnight/Most active 2.5000%        3.0000%\par Repurchase Overnight/Close       1.2500%        1.5000%\par            14-Day                1.5000%        1.5000%\par            3-Month               2.4375%        2.4375%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Government bond prices continued to rise, as yields in the secondary\par market dropped about three basis points, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A dealer at a foreign bank said that according to market talk, an\par offshore party had placed a large order for the issue due 2008 to\par initiate a three-month swap, in expectation that prices will continue to\par rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A dealer at another foreign bank said there was limited trade in\par government bonds auctioned in the primary market Wednesday, ahead of\par settlement Friday, and that yields dropped around two basis points from\par the already low average yield of the auction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said cash trading in the over-the-counter market Thursday\par should be at least as heavy as the THB8.28 billion recorded by the Thai\par Bond Dealing Center Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Thomas Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744;\par tom.fox@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7603at0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
