\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Flat; Likely To Be Range-Bound \b0\par\par\uc2 422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2000\par 03:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mostly steady early Monday, and will likely remain within tight trading bands amid caution ahead of the U.S. Federal Reserve's two-day policy meeting beginning Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  While the Fed is widely anticipated to leave interest rates unchanged, some market participants have already priced in the possibility of a 25-basis-point hike, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen's stability, after the Liberal Democratic Party-led coalition retained power in elections for Parliament's lower house Sunday, has provided little incentive for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to snap out of their recent trading ranges, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Trading in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to remain subdued as market participants are hesitant to open up new positions as the end of the half-year ends, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "They will unwind or maintain what they have," a dealer at an Asian bank said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's failure last week to convincingly breach key resistance levels of some Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may also push the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the lower end of the recent trading range in the short term, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah, the dollar has slipped to 8,645 rupiah around 0115 GMT (9:15 p.m. EDT), from IDR8,660 late Friday, after failing to stay above IDR8,700 late last week. The dollar will likely trade in the IDR8,600-IDR8,700 range for the rest of the day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at S$1.7323 against the Singapore dollar, up marginally from S$1.7311 late Friday, but well within its recent trading band of S$1.7300-S$1.7370. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is expected to trade within a narrow range of S$1.7300-S$1.7340 Monday, following unconfirmed rumors the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore might have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  around S$1.7340 last Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was at 39.085 baht, down marginally from THB39.100 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso has also moved little, at 42.865 pesos to the U.S. dollar, compared with Friday's close of PHP42.845. \par \par \uc2  Against the New Taiwan dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at NT$30.780, barely changed from Friday's close of NT$30.767. \par \par \uc2  In Seoul, the dollar has fallen to 1,118.50 won, from Friday's close of KRW1,119.40. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw6q0343g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
