\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Flat As Dollar Rally Loses Steam \b0\par\par\uc2 510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2000\par 13:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht ended flat in Asian spot trade Friday as the dollar's rally against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ran out of steam ahead of the weekend, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Rumors that Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the week helped to support the baht, but dealers said they saw no signs of any direct \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales this week. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 38.845 baht in Asian trading Friday, unchanged from Thursday. \par \par \uc2  At 0953 GMT (5:53 a.m. EDT), the dollar was slightly higher at THB38.885 in continuing London trade, but well within the THB38.75-THB39.00 range anticipated over the weekend. \par \par \uc2  The baht has weakened this week in line with most other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in anticipation of a 50 basis point increase in key U.S. interest rates next week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that under the circumstances, it was extremely unlikely that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would abandon a policy of nonintervention to support the baht. \par \par \uc2  "Do you think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants the baht stronger? I don't think so. With the yen and the Indonesian rupiah so much weaker, it would hurt the country's export competitiveness," a local dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said Bank of Thailand may have acted at times, however, to help bring about the short squeezes in offshore swap markets seen this week whenever the baht started to drop too quickly. \par \par \uc2  Higher premiums in swap markets make it more expensive for speculators to set up or maintain long-dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits the supply of baht in offshore swap markets through controls on baht outflows. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said purchase of dollars with baht obtained from settlements of the sale of Thai equities helped to push the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up during the day, but the Stock Exchange of Thailand Index recovered 2.7% to 345.67 points Friday after heavy losses earlier in the week. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose briefly to a high of THB39.045, but couldn't sustain those levels. \par \par \uc2  Money market rates were flat to lower, in line with low onshore swap rates. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is able maintains high liquidity and low interest rates in domestic markets because of its controls on baht outflows. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market     Term                  Friday         Thursday\par Interbank  Overnight/Most active 1.7500%        1.7500%\par Repurchase Overnight/Close       0.9375%        0.9375%\par            14-Day                1.5000%        1.5000%\par            3-Month               2.4375%        2.5625%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Government bond prices ended mostly higher Friday as investors\par returned to the market after a state enterprise bond auction produced a\par lower-than-expected yield, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The state Mass Rapid Transit Authority's auction Friday of a tranche\par of its 5-year bonds was awarded at a lower-than-expected yield, sending\par investors back to the secondary market, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bond auction result hasn't been released yet.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The trading report from the Thai Bond Dealing Center wasn't available\par due to technical difficulties at the center.\par \f28 \par \par \