\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Pummelled by rate-driven exodus. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Chisa Fujioka \par \uc2 1,055 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2000\par 11:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 11 (Reuters) - Asian markets were pummelled \par \par \uc2  on Thursday as expectations of an aggressive tightening in U.S. \par \par \uc2  interest rates continued to spin a vicious cycle, driving \par \par \uc2  regional stocks and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower. \par \par \uc2      "Besides the theme of higher U.S. interest rates, the focus \par \par \uc2  for Asian markets right now is also very bad equity market \par \par \uc2  performance that's leading to portfolio outflows out of Asian \par \par \uc2  countries," said Thio Chin Loo, strategist at BNP Paribas \par \par \uc2  Group. \par \par \uc2      "That's putting a dampener on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she told \par \par \uc2  Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2      The glum sentiment also depressed bond markets, kicking \par \par \uc2  Asian bond spreads wider as investors fled to save-haven U.S. \par \par \uc2  Treasuries. \par \par \uc2      All regional stock markets were lower, taking their cue \par \par \uc2  from weaker U.S. markets overnight that saw a sell-off in tech \par \par \uc2  shares spill over to more interest-rate sensitive sectors like \par \par \uc2  banks and brokers. \par \par \uc2  Losses were led by Tokyo's benchmark Nikkei average which \par \par \uc2  tumbled more than 4.5 percent, finishing below 17,000 for the \par \par \uc2  first time since September. \par \par \uc2  Traders blamed fears of more volatility in U.S. stocks in \par \par \uc2  coming sessions ahead of Tuesday's rate-setting meeting of the \par \par \uc2  U.S. Federal Open Market Committee. \par \par \uc2      Spared the potential damage were Hong Kong and South Korea, \par \par \uc2  both closed for public holidays. \par \par \uc2      REGIONAL \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  SHUNNED \par \par \uc2      Increased hedging activity and pre-payment of foreign loans \par \par \uc2  by Asian companies wary of further dollar strength were also \par \par \uc2  weighing on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , BNP-Paribas' Thio said. \par \par \uc2      The dollar rallied to two-month highs above 110 yen in late \par \par \uc2  Asian trade, helped by the Nikkei's descent. \par \par \uc2      Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some already plagued by domestic \par \par \uc2  concerns, were defenceless against the dollar, prompting some \par \par \uc2  central banks to step in. \par \par \uc2      A stream of dollar bids from offshore and corporate players \par \par \uc2  dragged the Indonesian rupiah to 8,420, its lowest level since \par \par \uc2  September 29. \par \par \uc2      Although talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sporadic \par \par \uc2  dollar profit-taking lifted the unit from its day low, the \par \par \uc2  market remained bearish. \par \par \uc2      The Sing dollar managed only a mild rebound amid market \par \par \uc2  rumours that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend it from \par \par \uc2  a 13-month low. \par \par \uc2      THAI BAHT'S WOES PERSIST \par \par \uc2      Bangkok dealers said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  in offshore \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the baht after \par \par \uc2  it fell through 39.00 per dollar. \par \par \uc2      But despite the unconfirmed action, the baht remained \par \par \uc2  around five-month lows, with some dealers forecasting it would \par \par \uc2  slip again to test next support at 39.20. \par \par \uc2      The 39.20 per dollar level marks the 50 percent Fibonacci \par \par \uc2  retracement of the dollar's September 28 to January 3 decline, \par \par \uc2  chartists said. \par \par \uc2      "There is no good reason for corporates to shoulder rising \par \par \uc2  costs as a result of a widening gap in global interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The hike in U.S. interest rates put pressure on Thai corporates \par \par \uc2  to rush to repay foreign debts," Anusorn Tamjai, macroeconomist \par \par \uc2  at Citibank in Bangkok said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said denial by the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and finance \par \par \uc2  minister that financial authorities intended to impose capital \par \par \uc2  controls gave psychological support. \par \par \uc2  Thai Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda and the Bank \par \par \uc2  of Thailand on Thursday denied rumours that they planned to \par \par \uc2  impose capital controls to help prevent further falls for the \par \par \uc2  baht. \par \par \uc2  KOREA SEES SCANT INFLATION THREAT \par \par \uc2  Korea's Finance Minister Lee Hun-jai attempted to calm \par \par \uc2  fears of an overheating economy, saying inflationary pressure \par \par \uc2  was largely absent despite expectations GDP growth would exceed \par \par \uc2  an originally forecast six percent this year. \par \par \uc2  "We are now looking for a solid real GDP growth this year, \par \par \uc2  most likely higher than the originally expected six percent," \par \par \uc2  Lee told an annual meeting of the Asia Society in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2      "Better still, we see no clear signs of overheating while \par \par \uc2  significant inflationary pressure is largely absent," he said. \par \par \uc2      South Korea's GDP grew 10.7 percent in 1999, which had \par \par \uc2  sparked market worries of a pick-up in inflation. \par \par \uc2      Lee said inflation this year would be within the originally \par \par \uc2  estimated three percent, while a strong export performance \par \par \uc2  would yield a continued trade surplus. \par \par \uc2      But worries for the economy seemed far from over as local \par \par \uc2  media reported the country may need an additional 42 trillion \par \par \uc2  won to complete financial sector restructuring by the end of \par \par \uc2  this year. \par \par \uc2  Maeil Business Newspaper quoted state-funded Korea \par \par \uc2  Institute of Finance as saying South Korea had already spent 86 \par \par \uc2  trillion won since the 1997 economic crisis to clean up the \par \par \uc2  financial sector. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0925 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     109.74\tab  109.40\tab    -0.31\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7260\tab  1.7297\tab    +0.21\par  Taiwan dlr    30.752\tab  30.697\tab    -0.18\par  Korean won   1112.50\tab 1109.00\tab    -0.31\par  Baht\tab      38.90\tab   38.89\tab    -0.03\par  Peso\tab      41.35\tab   41.37\tab    +0.05\par  Rupiah\tab  8390.00\tab 8190.00\tab    -2.38\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.74\tab  102.21\tab    -6.86\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7260\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.59\par  Taiwan dlr    30.752\tab  31.380\tab    +2.04\par  Korean won   1112.50\tab 1135.00\tab    +2.02\par  Baht\tab      38.90\tab   37.45\tab    -3.73\par  Peso\tab      41.35\tab   40.20\tab    -2.78\par  Rupiah\tab  8390.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -16.87\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7997\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f