\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Dealers say Thai cenbank props up baht. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kettiya Jittapong \par \uc2 621 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2000\par 14:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the weakening baht on Thursday, while the stock market continued its week-long decline. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said baht buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 39 to the dollar pushed the unit back above the key support level, and by late Asian trade it had recovered to 38.88/93. \par \par \uc2  But it remained at five-month lows and dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have only a limited impact. Several forecast the baht could slip back again to test its next support at 39.20. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  assistant governor Chetthavee Charoenpitak said he had not been told of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but three dealers at major Thai banks confirmed they had seen the bank in the market. \par \par \uc2  "Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there is an attempt by offshore parties to drag the baht down and test support of 39 again," said a dealer at major Thai bank. \par \par \uc2  "Some exporters entered market to check the rate but most of them are waiting to take profit from recent gains of dollar at above 39." \par \par \uc2  Satian Tantanasarit, chief dealer at DBS Thai Danu Bank, said he expected the volatility of the baht to be reduced next week, when the U.S. Federal Reserve is expected to raise interest rates 50 basis points. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht weakness was due to sustained dollar buying by offshore parties and corporates amid concerns about fund outflows and the possible U.S. rate hike. \par \par \uc2  RUMOUR DENIALS PROVIDE PSYCHOLOGICAL SUPPORT \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a denial by the Bank of Thailand and Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda that the authorities intended to impose capital controls gave psychological support. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the rumours, Tarrin replied: "They are wrong." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  assistant governor Chetthavee Charoenpitak told reporters the baht's weakness was in line with movements in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and due to external factors and the stock market. \par \par \uc2  It was another gloomy day for stocks as investors sold telecoms, media and technology, as well as banks. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark composite SET index ended down 6.99 points, or 2.03 percent, at 336.54, its lowest close for 14 months. It closed at 333.28 on March 10, 1999. \par \par \uc2  This week alone, the SET has lost 11.43 percent, in an average daily turnover of 2.33 billion baht. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said continued volatility in nearly all regional and global markets had helped erode the confidence of Thai retail investors, who have joined foreign investors as sellers. \par \par \uc2  A stock analyst at Merrill Lynch said Thailand was now referred to as one of the "TIP" countries - Thailand, Indonesia and Philippines. "It's a sector in which there is very little interest from foreign investors," he said. \par \par \uc2  Its reform process needed to be speeded up if it was to get back on to the radar screens of institutional investors, he said. \par \par \uc2  Chartists said the next target for dollar/baht was the 39.20 level, a 50 percent Fibonacci retracement of the dollar's September 28 to January 3 decline on the daily chart. \par \par \uc2  "39.20 is actually the dollar resistance. It's not at this level (39.00)," said a baht trader. \par \par \uc2  A break beyond 39.20 would put the dollar on track for a further rise towards 39.80 baht. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were bearish towards the Thai unit near-term, given expectations of persistent corporate dollar demand to accelerate debt repayment ahead of the Tuesday Fed meeting. \par \par \uc2  "It is a story of fund movements," said Anusorn Tamjai, macro economist at Citibank in Bangkok. "Foreigners are moving their money out of the Thai market as other global markets yield more attractive returns. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5b00pp0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
