\par\par \b \uc2  Thai c. bank says no baht  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2000\par 11:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 4 (Reuters) - A senior Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Thursday the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to shore up the baht despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's setbacks this week. \par \par \uc2  Thirachai Phuvanat-naranubala, assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, told reporters the Bank of Thailand closely watched the baht's movement but it had not made any efforts to halt its retreat against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The baht has eased along with the weaker euro and yen...we have not seen any unusual \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not stepped in to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but we are closely monitoring them," he said. \par \par \uc2  The baht, tracking most bearish regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fell to near a five-month low of around 38.52 per dollar on Thursday from around 38.05 late last week. \par \par \uc2  Thirachai said Thai market players chose to retain their dollar positions this week partly in anticipation of rate hikes by the U.S. Federal Reserves later this month. \par \par \uc2  ((Vithoon Amorn, Bangkok newsroom 662-6375500 ext 412 \par \par \uc2  email: bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw54014un\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
