\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Higher; Investors Take Profit On Dlr Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2000\par 11:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht closed higher against the dollar Friday in Asian spot trade as both offshore and local investors took profits on the recent dollar strength. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 37.315 baht in Asian trade, down from THB37.40 Thursday, and sharply off its intraday high at THB37.62. \par \par \uc2  Selling pressure was seen once the dollar hit THB37.50, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Most investors had bought the dollar from the THB37.30 level on, so THB37.50 was high enough to take profit," said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Fears of a U.S. rate hike pulled down Wall Street markets earlier in the week and caused regional equities markets to tumble, which pushed down regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The baht weakened beyond the THB37.40 level, from THB36.90 early this week. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said late Friday afternoon that the dollar at THB37.40 won't adversely affect \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exports, and that it wouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  the market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the baht to trade in a range of THB37.15 and THB37.75 next week. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Chanyaporn Chanjaroen; 662-266-0744;\par chanyaporn.chanjaroen@dowjones.com\par -0- 07/01/00 10-19G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw170052e\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx